window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-10-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-10-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 10 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000073281","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"If P + Q means P is the brother of Q, P − Q means P is the mother of Q, and P × Q means P is the sister of Q.<br><br>Which of the following means M is the maternal uncle of R? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि P + Q का अर्थ है P, Q का भाई है, P − Q का अर्थ है P, Q की माता है, और P × Q का अर्थ है P, Q की बहन है।<br><br>निम्नलिखित में से किसका अर्थ है कि M, R का मामा है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"M − K − R"},"2":{"en":"M − R + K"},"3":{"en":"M + K × R"},"4":{"en":"M + K − R"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"108\" y=\"34\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M172 54V76M172 76V88M122 24H172M122 24V34M172 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"122\" y=\"48\">M+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"48\">K−</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"102\">R</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>M + K − R: M is the brother of K, and K is the mother of R, so M is R's maternal uncle.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): M + K − R.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"108\" y=\"34\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M172 54V76M172 76V88M122 24H172M122 24V34M172 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"122\" y=\"48\">M+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"48\">K−</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"102\">R</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>M + K − R: M, K का भाई है तथा K, R की माता है, अतः M, R का मामा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): M + K − R है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000073282","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"How many such T are there in the sequence which are immediately preceded by P but not immediately followed by R?<br>Sequence:<br>PTQTPTRPTPSTRPTPQT [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अनुक्रम में ऐसे कितने T हैं जिनके ठीक पहले P है लेकिन ठीक बाद R नहीं है?<br>अनुक्रम:<br>PTQTPTRPTPSTRPTPQT [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Positions: P1 T2 Q3 T4 P5 T6 R7 P8 T9 P10 S11 T12 R13 P14 T15 P16 Q17 T18<br>T immediately preceded by P: T2 (PTQ), T6 (PTR), T9 (PTP), T15 (PTP)<br>Leaving out T6, which is followed by R, the required T are T2, T9 and T15 → 3<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.</b><br><br><b>Note:</b> SSC's official answer key marked option (2): 2 as correct, but the sequence has 3 such T (PTQ, PTP, PTP). This is a <b>bonus question</b>.","hi":"स्थान: P1 T2 Q3 T4 P5 T6 R7 P8 T9 P10 S11 T12 R13 P14 T15 P16 Q17 T18<br>जिन T के ठीक पहले P है: T2 (PTQ), T6 (PTR), T9 (PTP), T15 (PTP)<br>T6 के ठीक बाद R है, उसे छोड़कर आवश्यक T हैं T2, T9 और T15 → 3<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 है।</b><br><br><b>नोट:</b> SSC की आधिकारिक उत्तर कुंजी में विकल्प (2): 2 को सही बताया गया है, परंतु अनुक्रम में ऐसे 3 T (PTQ, PTP, PTP) हैं। यह एक <b>बोनस प्रश्न</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000073283","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"In a group of five members, P, Q, R, S, and T, Q is the daughter of P. R is the son of Q. S is the brother of P. T is the mother of S. How is T related to R? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पाँच सदस्यों P, Q, R, S और T के एक समूह में, Q, P की पुत्री है। R, Q का पुत्र है। S, P का भाई है। T, S की माता है। T का R से क्या संबंध है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Maternal Great-grandmother","hi":"परनानी"},"2":{"en":"Paternal Grandmother","hi":"दादी"},"3":{"en":"Mother","hi":"माता"},"4":{"en":"Paternal Aunt","hi":"बुआ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"216\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 216\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"133\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"109\" y=\"170\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M146 28V50M122 50H171M122 50V62M171 50V62M122 82V104M122 104V116M122 136V158M122 158V170\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"22\">T−</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"76\">P</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"76\">S+</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"130\">Q−</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"184\">R+</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"211\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>T is the mother of P, whose daughter Q is R's mother, so T is R's maternal great-grandmother.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Maternal Great-grandmother.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"216\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 216\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"133\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"109\" y=\"170\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M146 28V50M122 50H171M122 50V62M171 50V62M122 82V104M122 104V116M122 136V158M122 158V170\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"22\">T−</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"76\">P</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"76\">S+</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"130\">Q−</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"184\">R+</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"211\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>T, P की माता है और P की पुत्री Q, R की माता है, अतः T, R की परनानी है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): परनानी है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000073284","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार एक निश्चित पैटर्न का अनुसरण करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और तदनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"7"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Column-wise: (first × second) ÷ third = fourth<br>8 × 5 ÷ 2 = 20, 6 × 9 ÷ 3 = 18<br>4 × 3 ÷ ? = 6 ⇒ ? = 2<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ-वार: (पहली × दूसरी) ÷ तीसरी = चौथी<br>8 × 5 ÷ 2 = 20, 6 × 9 ÷ 3 = 18<br>4 × 3 ÷ ? = 6 ⇒ ? = 2<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000073285","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">35</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार एक निश्चित पैटर्न का अनुसरण करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और तदनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">45</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">35</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">30</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14"},"2":{"en":"20"},"3":{"en":"24"},"4":{"en":"36"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Column-wise: first − second + third = fourth<br>20 − 14 + 6 = 12, 45 − 30 + 15 = 30<br>35 − 25 + 10 = 20<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 20.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ-वार: पहली − दूसरी + तीसरी = चौथी<br>20 − 14 + 6 = 12, 45 − 30 + 15 = 30<br>35 − 25 + 10 = 20<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 20 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000073286","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the alternative number in the series.<br><br>7, 4, 49, 9, 441, 16, 4851, 25, ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रृंखला में वैकल्पिक संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए।<br><br>7, 4, 49, 9, 441, 16, 4851, 25, ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"67903"},"2":{"en":"63063"},"3":{"en":"74890"},"4":{"en":"68909"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Two series alternate.<br>4, 9, 16, 25 are squares.<br>7 × 7 = 49, 49 × 9 = 441, 441 × 11 = 4851, 4851 × 13 = 63063<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 63063.</b>","hi":"दो श्रृंखलाएँ एकांतर रूप में हैं।<br>4, 9, 16, 25 वर्ग हैं।<br>7 × 7 = 49, 49 × 9 = 441, 441 × 11 = 4851, 4851 × 13 = 63063<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 63063 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000073287","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"<b>Using the codes given below, answer the question that follows.</b><br>1. M % N means M is the son of N.<br>2. M @ N means M is the sister of N.<br>3. M &#36; N means M is the father of N.<br>Which of the following expressions given in the options shows the relation that E is the paternal grandfather of C? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>नीचे दिए गए कूटों का प्रयोग करके आगे दिए गए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।</b><br>1. M % N का अर्थ है M, N का पुत्र है।<br>2. M @ N का अर्थ है M, N की बहन है।<br>3. M &#36; N का अर्थ है M, N का पिता है।<br>विकल्पों में दिए गए निम्नलिखित व्यंजकों में से कौन-सा यह संबंध दर्शाता है कि E, C का दादा है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"C % B @ F &#36; E"},"2":{"en":"E &#36; B &#36; C @ F"},"3":{"en":"E % B &#36; F @ C"},"4":{"en":"C @ B % F &#36; E"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"135\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"112\" y=\"116\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M148 28V50M148 50V62M148 82V104M125 104H171M125 104V116M171 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"148\" y=\"22\">E+</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"76\">B+</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"130\">C−</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"130\">F</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>E &#36; B &#36; C @ F: E is the father of B and B is the father of C, so E is C's paternal grandfather.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): E &#36; B &#36; C @ F.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"162\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 162\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"135\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"112\" y=\"116\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M148 28V50M148 50V62M148 82V104M125 104H171M125 104V116M171 104V116\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"148\" y=\"22\">E+</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"76\">B+</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"130\">C−</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"130\">F</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"157\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>E &#36; B &#36; C @ F: E, B का पिता है तथा B, C का पिता है, अतः E, C का दादा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): E &#36; B &#36; C @ F है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000073288","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The roll number of a specific batch follows the rule: The sum of the first two digits must equal the sum of the last two digits. Find the inconsistent roll number. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक विशेष बैच का रोल नंबर इस नियम का पालन करता है: पहले दो अंकों का योग अंतिम दो अंकों के योग के बराबर होना चाहिए। असंगत रोल नंबर ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"63482109"},"2":{"en":"57124939"},"3":{"en":"92317429"},"4":{"en":"48512968"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"63482109: 6 + 3 = 9 = 0 + 9 ✓<br>57124939: 5 + 7 = 12 = 3 + 9 ✓<br>92317429: 9 + 2 = 11 = 2 + 9 ✓<br>48512968: 4 + 8 = 12 ≠ 6 + 8 = 14 ✗<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 48512968.</b>","hi":"63482109: 6 + 3 = 9 = 0 + 9 ✓<br>57124939: 5 + 7 = 12 = 3 + 9 ✓<br>92317429: 9 + 2 = 11 = 2 + 9 ✓<br>48512968: 4 + 8 = 12 ≠ 6 + 8 = 14 ✗<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 48512968 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000073289","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या-युग्म का चयन कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"41, 1722"},"2":{"en":"33, 1122"},"3":{"en":"22, 504"},"4":{"en":"15, 240"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Rule: second = n² + n<br>41² + 41 = 1722, 33² + 33 = 1122, 15² + 15 = 240<br>22² + 22 = 506, not 504<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 22, 504.</b>","hi":"नियम: दूसरी = n² + n<br>41² + 41 = 1722, 33² + 33 = 1122, 15² + 15 = 240<br>22² + 22 = 506 है, 504 नहीं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 22, 504 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000073290","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"<b>Read the question carefully and choose the most appropriate option.</b><br>You are the head of a housing society. Children are playing cricket in the parking area, and some residents are worried about damage to their vehicles. What would you do? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>प्रश्न को ध्यान से पढ़िए और सबसे उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।</b><br>आप एक आवास सोसाइटी के प्रमुख हैं। बच्चे पार्किंग क्षेत्र में क्रिकेट खेल रहे हैं, और कुछ निवासी अपने वाहनों को नुकसान को लेकर चिंतित हैं। आप क्या करेंगे? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ban all outdoor games immediately without consulting any residents first.","hi":"किसी भी निवासी से पहले परामर्श किए बिना सभी बाहरी खेलों पर तुरंत प्रतिबंध लगाना।"},"2":{"en":"Ignore the complaints and allow the situation to continue unchanged.","hi":"शिकायतों को अनदेखा करना और स्थिति को बिना बदलाव के चलने देना।"},"3":{"en":"Avoid involvement because disagreements among residents are quite common.","hi":"दखल देने से बचना क्योंकि निवासियों के बीच असहमति काफ़ी आम है।"},"4":{"en":"Arrange a meeting and identify a safer area for games to reduce damage.","hi":"एक बैठक आयोजित करना और नुकसान कम करने के लिए खेलों हेतु एक सुरक्षित स्थान तय करना।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A meeting balances both concerns: children can still play and vehicles stay safe.<br>Banning, ignoring or avoiding the issue does not solve it.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Arrange a meeting and identify a safer area for games to reduce damage.</b>","hi":"बैठक दोनों चिंताओं में संतुलन बनाती है: बच्चे खेल भी सकें और वाहन सुरक्षित रहें।<br>प्रतिबंध, अनदेखी या दखल न देना समस्या हल नहीं करता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): एक बैठक आयोजित करना और नुकसान कम करने के लिए खेलों हेतु एक सुरक्षित स्थान तय करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000073291","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the best alternative.<br><br>α1 : β4 :: γ9 : ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सबसे उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br><br>α1 : β4 :: γ9 : ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"δ12"},"2":{"en":"δ16"},"3":{"en":"ε16"},"4":{"en":"δ10"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Greek letters in order: α (1st), β (2nd), γ (3rd), δ (4th).<br>Number = square of the position: 1, 4, 9, 16<br>So γ9 : δ16<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): δ16.</b>","hi":"ग्रीक अक्षर क्रम से: α (पहला), β (दूसरा), γ (तीसरा), δ (चौथा)।<br>संख्या = स्थान का वर्ग: 1, 4, 9, 16<br>अतः γ9 : δ16<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): δ16 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000073292","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of the question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br><br>MARKET : LZQJDS :: BRIDGE : ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्न चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आना चाहिए?<br><br>MARKET : LZQJDS :: BRIDGE : ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"AQHCFD"},"2":{"en":"AQHCFE"},"3":{"en":"AQHCFW"},"4":{"en":"BQHCFD"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"MARKET → LZQJDS: each letter −1<br>BRIDGE: B−1 = A, R−1 = Q, I−1 = H, D−1 = C, G−1 = F, E−1 = D → AQHCFD<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): AQHCFD.</b>","hi":"MARKET → LZQJDS: प्रत्येक अक्षर −1<br>BRIDGE: B−1 = A, R−1 = Q, I−1 = H, D−1 = C, G−1 = F, E−1 = D → AQHCFD<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): AQHCFD है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000073293","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If the expression 24 ÷ 6 × 3 + 4 − 2 = X is computed, what happens to the value of X if the division sign is replaced by multiplication? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि व्यंजक 24 ÷ 6 × 3 + 4 − 2 = X की गणना की जाए, तो भाग के चिह्न को गुणा से बदलने पर X के मान का क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increases by 280","hi":"280 बढ़ जाता है"},"2":{"en":"Decreases by 12","hi":"12 घट जाता है"},"3":{"en":"Increases by 416","hi":"416 बढ़ जाता है"},"4":{"en":"Increases by 420","hi":"420 बढ़ जाता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Original: 24 ÷ 6 × 3 + 4 − 2 = 12 + 2 = 14<br>New: 24 × 6 × 3 + 4 − 2 = 432 + 2 = 434<br>Increase = 434 − 14 = 420<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Increases by 420.</b>","hi":"मूल: 24 ÷ 6 × 3 + 4 − 2 = 12 + 2 = 14<br>नया: 24 × 6 × 3 + 4 − 2 = 432 + 2 = 434<br>वृद्धि = 434 − 14 = 420<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 420 बढ़ जाता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000073294","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>In a one-day cricket match, the total runs scored by a team were 200, out of which spinners made 150.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The team had 75% spinners.<br>II. Fast bowlers outperformed the spinners. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए गए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और तय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष, यदि कोई हो, कथन का तार्किक रूप से अनुसरण करता/करते है/हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक एकदिवसीय क्रिकेट मैच में, एक टीम द्वारा बनाए गए कुल रन 200 थे, जिनमें से 150 स्पिनरों ने बनाए।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. टीम में 75% स्पिनर थे।<br>II. तेज़ गेंदबाज़ों ने स्पिनरों से बेहतर प्रदर्शन किया। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II अनुसरण करता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"75% of the runs came from spinners; this says nothing about how many players were spinners, so I does not follow.<br>Spinners scored more runs, so II is false.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither conclusion I nor II follows.</b>","hi":"75% रन स्पिनरों ने बनाए; इससे यह पता नहीं चलता कि कितने खिलाड़ी स्पिनर थे, अतः I अनुसरण नहीं करता।<br>स्पिनरों ने अधिक रन बनाए, अतः II गलत है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II अनुसरण करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000073295","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"In the following question a statement is given followed by some assumptions. Read the assumptions carefully and choose the appropriate option.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Before finalizing the budget for the community project, please review all expenditure estimates.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. The estimates may contain errors.<br>II. A realistic budget is important for the project. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ पूर्वधारणाएँ दी गई हैं। पूर्वधारणाओं को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सामुदायिक परियोजना का बजट अंतिम रूप देने से पहले, कृपया सभी व्यय अनुमानों की समीक्षा करें।<br><b>पूर्वधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. अनुमानों में त्रुटियाँ हो सकती हैं।<br>II. परियोजना के लिए यथार्थवादी बजट महत्वपूर्ण है। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I is implicit.","hi":"केवल I निहित है।"},"2":{"en":"Only II is implicit.","hi":"केवल II निहित है।"},"3":{"en":"Neither I nor II is implicit.","hi":"न तो I और न ही II निहित है।"},"4":{"en":"Both I and II are implicit.","hi":"I और II दोनों निहित हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Asking for a review assumes the estimates may have errors (I).<br>It also assumes that a realistic budget matters for the project (II).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Both I and II are implicit.</b>","hi":"समीक्षा के लिए कहना यह मानता है कि अनुमानों में त्रुटियाँ हो सकती हैं (I)।<br>यह भी मानता है कि परियोजना के लिए यथार्थवादी बजट महत्वपूर्ण है (II)।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): I और II दोनों निहित हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000073296","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If ‘★’ means +, ‘△’ means −, ‘♦’ means ×, and ‘○’ means ÷, find [(144 ○ 12) ♦ (7 ★ 5)] △ [(18 ♦ 2) ★ (36 ○ 6)]. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि ‘★’ का अर्थ +, ‘△’ का अर्थ −, ‘♦’ का अर्थ × और ‘○’ का अर्थ ÷ है, तो [(144 ○ 12) ♦ (7 ★ 5)] △ [(18 ♦ 2) ★ (36 ○ 6)] ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"84"},"2":{"en":"96"},"3":{"en":"102"},"4":{"en":"108"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"[(144 ÷ 12) × (7 + 5)] − [(18 × 2) + (36 ÷ 6)]<br>= (12 × 12) − (36 + 6)<br>= 144 − 42 = 102<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 102.</b>","hi":"[(144 ÷ 12) × (7 + 5)] − [(18 × 2) + (36 ÷ 6)]<br>= (12 × 12) − (36 + 6)<br>= 144 − 42 = 102<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 102 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000073297","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"<b>Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided. If any exception applies, identify the authority to whom the case should be referred.</b><br><b>Criteria for Project Lead Promotion:</b><br><b>(i)</b> Must have led at least 2 projects.<br><b>(ii)</b> Must have an 'Excellent' performance rating.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br><b>Exception (A):</b> If the candidate has led only 1 project but has an 'Exceptional' performance rating, refer the case to the Operations Head.<br><b>Exception (B):</b> If the candidate has led 2 projects but has a 'Good' performance rating and 5 years of tenure, refer the case to the HR Committee.<br><b>Case:</b> The candidate has led 1 project and has an 'Exceptional' performance rating. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>दी गई शर्तों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और दिए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित कीजिए। यदि कोई अपवाद लागू होता है, तो उस प्राधिकारी की पहचान कीजिए जिसे मामला भेजा जाना चाहिए।</b><br><b>प्रोजेक्ट लीड पदोन्नति के मानदंड:</b><br><b>(i)</b> कम से कम 2 परियोजनाओं का नेतृत्व किया हो।<br><b>(ii)</b> 'उत्कृष्ट' (Excellent) प्रदर्शन रेटिंग होनी चाहिए।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br><b>अपवाद (A):</b> यदि उम्मीदवार ने केवल 1 परियोजना का नेतृत्व किया है लेकिन उसकी प्रदर्शन रेटिंग 'असाधारण' (Exceptional) है, तो मामला संचालन प्रमुख को भेजें।<br><b>अपवाद (B):</b> यदि उम्मीदवार ने 2 परियोजनाओं का नेतृत्व किया है लेकिन उसकी प्रदर्शन रेटिंग 'अच्छी' (Good) है और 5 वर्ष का कार्यकाल है, तो मामला HR समिति को भेजें।<br><b>मामला:</b> उम्मीदवार ने 1 परियोजना का नेतृत्व किया है और उसकी प्रदर्शन रेटिंग 'असाधारण' है। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Promotion to be approved","hi":"पदोन्नति स्वीकृत की जाए"},"2":{"en":"Promotion to be denied","hi":"पदोन्नति अस्वीकार की जाए"},"3":{"en":"Refer the case to the Operations Head","hi":"मामला संचालन प्रमुख को भेजा जाए"},"4":{"en":"Case to be referred to the HR Committee","hi":"मामला HR समिति को भेजा जाए"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Only 1 project is led, so criterion (i) fails.<br>With an 'Exceptional' rating, Exception (A) applies → refer to the Operations Head.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Refer the case to the Operations Head.</b>","hi":"केवल 1 परियोजना का नेतृत्व किया, अतः मानदंड (i) पूरा नहीं होता।<br>'असाधारण' रेटिंग के साथ अपवाद (A) लागू → संचालन प्रमुख को भेजें।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): मामला संचालन प्रमुख को भेजा जाए है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000073298","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"AIRCRAFT\" is written as \"1irCRA6T\". How will \"BIRTHDAY\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में, \"AIRCRAFT\" को \"1irCRA6T\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"BIRTHDAY\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2irTHD1Y"},"2":{"en":"2iRtHD1Y"},"3":{"en":"2irTHdLY"},"4":{"en":"2IrThD1Y"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"1st and 7th letters → their alphabet positions; 2nd and 3rd → small letters; 4th, 5th, 6th and 8th unchanged.<br>BIRTHDAY: B → 2, i, r, T, H, D, A → 1, Y → 2irTHD1Y<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2irTHD1Y.</b>","hi":"पहला और सातवाँ अक्षर → उनका वर्णमाला स्थान; दूसरा और तीसरा → छोटे अक्षर; चौथा, पाँचवाँ, छठा और आठवाँ अपरिवर्तित।<br>BIRTHDAY: B → 2, i, r, T, H, D, A → 1, Y → 2irTHD1Y<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2irTHD1Y है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000073299","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question two statements are given and these statements are followed by two conclusions. You have to take the given two statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the two given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Some mobiles are gadgets.<br>Some gadgets are electronics.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All electronics are gadgets.<br>II. Some electronics are gadget [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दो कथन और उनके बाद दो निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। आपको दिए गए दोनों कथनों को सत्य मानना है, भले ही वे सामान्य रूप से ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों। निष्कर्षों को पढ़िए और फिर तय कीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा दोनों कथनों का तार्किक रूप से अनुसरण करता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ मोबाइल गैजेट हैं।<br>कुछ गैजेट इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स गैजेट हैं।<br>II. कुछ इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स गैजेट हैं। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"4":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\"Some gadgets are electronics\" converts to \"Some electronics are gadgets\" → II follows.<br>\"All electronics are gadgets\" is not certain → I does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"\"कुछ गैजेट इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स हैं\" का रूपांतरण \"कुछ इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स गैजेट हैं\" है → II अनुसरण करता है।<br>\"सभी इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स गैजेट हैं\" निश्चित नहीं → I नहीं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000073300","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question, three statements are given followed by three conclusions. Consider the statements to be true even if they differ from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions carefully and decide which of the conclusions logically follow from the given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Some cats are dogs.<br>All dogs are animals.<br>No animal is a plant.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Some cats are animals.<br>II. All cats are animals.<br>III. Some animals are not plants. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में तीन कथन और उनके बाद तीन निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वे सामान्य रूप से ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न हों। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और तय कीजिए कि कौन-से निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों का तार्किक रूप से अनुसरण करते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ बिल्लियाँ कुत्ते हैं।<br>सभी कुत्ते जानवर हैं।<br>कोई भी जानवर पौधा नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कुछ बिल्लियाँ जानवर हैं।<br>II. सभी बिल्लियाँ जानवर हैं।<br>III. कुछ जानवर पौधे नहीं हैं। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Both conclusions I and III follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और III दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusions II and III follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष II और III दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"All conclusions follow","hi":"सभी निष्कर्ष अनुसरण करते हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Some cats are dogs and all dogs are animals → Some cats are animals (I).<br>Not all cats are known to be animals → II does not follow.<br>No animal is a plant → Some animals are not plants (III).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Both conclusions I and III follow.</b>","hi":"कुछ बिल्लियाँ कुत्ते हैं और सभी कुत्ते जानवर हैं → कुछ बिल्लियाँ जानवर हैं (I)।<br>सभी बिल्लियों का जानवर होना ज्ञात नहीं → II नहीं।<br>कोई जानवर पौधा नहीं → कुछ जानवर पौधे नहीं हैं (III)।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): निष्कर्ष I और III दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000073301","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"Direction:<br>Choose the best course of action.<br><br>A financial institution observes unusual transaction patterns that may indicate emerging fraud techniques, although no confirmed losses have occurred. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निर्देश:<br>सबसे उपयुक्त कार्यवाही चुनिए।<br><br>एक वित्तीय संस्था असामान्य लेनदेन पैटर्न देखती है जो उभरती धोखाधड़ी तकनीकों का संकेत हो सकते हैं, हालाँकि अभी तक कोई पुष्ट नुकसान नहीं हुआ है। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Wait for confirmed financial losses before investigating further patterns.","hi":"आगे के पैटर्न की जाँच से पहले पुष्ट वित्तीय नुकसान की प्रतीक्षा करना।"},"2":{"en":"Publicly announce fraud concerns before conducting any internal verification.","hi":"कोई आंतरिक सत्यापन किए बिना धोखाधड़ी की चिंताओं की सार्वजनिक घोषणा करना।"},"3":{"en":"Conduct preventive investigations and strengthen monitoring systems proactively.","hi":"निवारक जाँच करना और सक्रिय रूप से निगरानी प्रणालियों को मज़बूत करना।"},"4":{"en":"Restrict all customer transactions until the source of concern is identified.","hi":"चिंता के स्रोत की पहचान होने तक सभी ग्राहक लेनदेन पर रोक लगाना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Early warning signs call for prevention, not waiting or panic.<br>Investigating and tightening monitoring stops fraud without harming customers.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Conduct preventive investigations and strengthen monitoring systems proactively.</b>","hi":"शुरुआती चेतावनी संकेतों पर रोकथाम ज़रूरी है, न कि प्रतीक्षा या घबराहट।<br>जाँच और सख्त निगरानी ग्राहकों को नुकसान पहुँचाए बिना धोखाधड़ी रोकती है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): निवारक जाँच करना और सक्रिय रूप से निगरानी प्रणालियों को मज़बूत करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000073302","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question, three statements are given, followed by two conclusions. Consider the statements to be true even if they differ from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions carefully and decide which of the conclusions logically follow from the given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Only a few coats are shirts.<br>Some shirts are pants.<br>No pants are socks.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All coats can be shirts is a possibility.<br>II. All shirts can be coats is a possibility. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में तीन कथन और उनके बाद दो निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वे सामान्य रूप से ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न हों। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और तय कीजिए कि कौन-से निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों का तार्किक रूप से अनुसरण करते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>केवल कुछ कोट शर्ट हैं।<br>कुछ शर्ट पैंट हैं।<br>कोई भी पैंट मोज़ा नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी कोट शर्ट हो सकते हैं, यह एक संभावना है।<br>II. सभी शर्ट कोट हो सकती हैं, यह एक संभावना है। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I अनुसरण करता है"},"2":{"en":"Either conclusion I or conclusion II follows","hi":"या तो निष्कर्ष I या निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\"Only a few coats are shirts\" means some coats are definitely not shirts → I is not possible.<br>Nothing stops all shirts from being coats → II is possible.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"\"केवल कुछ कोट शर्ट हैं\" का अर्थ है कुछ कोट निश्चित रूप से शर्ट नहीं हैं → I संभव नहीं।<br>सभी शर्टों के कोट होने में कोई बाधा नहीं → II संभव है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल निष्कर्ष II अनुसरण करता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000073303","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>LOM, ISJ, FWG, CAD, ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई श्रृंखला के पैटर्न का अध्ययन कीजिए और श्रृंखला में अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>LOM, ISJ, FWG, CAD, ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ZEA"},"2":{"en":"VDA"},"3":{"en":"WDA"},"4":{"en":"VCB"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"1st letter: L → I → F → C → Z (−3)<br>2nd letter: O → S → W → A → E (+4)<br>3rd letter: M → J → G → D → A (−3)<br>Next = ZEA<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ZEA.</b>","hi":"पहला अक्षर: L → I → F → C → Z (−3)<br>दूसरा अक्षर: O → S → W → A → E (+4)<br>तीसरा अक्षर: M → J → G → D → A (−3)<br>अगला = ZEA<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ZEA है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000073304","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br><br>Theodolite : Surveyor :: Stethoscope : ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्दों को अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्दों के रूप में माना जाना चाहिए और उन्हें शब्द में अक्षरों की संख्या/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर एक-दूसरे से संबंधित नहीं किया जाना चाहिए।)<br><br>थियोडोलाइट : सर्वेक्षक :: स्टेथोस्कोप : ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Physician","hi":"चिकित्सक"},"2":{"en":"Engineer","hi":"इंजीनियर"},"3":{"en":"Chemist","hi":"रसायनज्ञ"},"4":{"en":"Astronomer","hi":"खगोलशास्त्री"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A theodolite is the instrument used by a surveyor.<br>A stethoscope is the instrument used by a physician.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Physician.</b>","hi":"थियोडोलाइट सर्वेक्षक द्वारा प्रयुक्त उपकरण है।<br>स्टेथोस्कोप चिकित्सक द्वारा प्रयुक्त उपकरण है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): चिकित्सक है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000073305","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In each of the following questions, four options have been given, of which three are alike in some way and one is different. Choose the odd one out. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रत्येक प्रश्न में चार विकल्प दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी प्रकार समान हैं और एक भिन्न है। असंगत विकल्प चुनिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mexico – Peso","hi":"मेक्सिको – पेसो"},"2":{"en":"Philippines – Peso","hi":"फ़िलीपींस – पेसो"},"3":{"en":"Colombia – Peso","hi":"कोलंबिया – पेसो"},"4":{"en":"Brazil – Peso","hi":"ब्राज़ील – पेसो"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Mexico, the Philippines and Colombia use the Peso.<br>Brazil's currency is the Real, so this pair is wrong.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Brazil – Peso.</b>","hi":"मेक्सिको, फ़िलीपींस और कोलंबिया की मुद्रा पेसो है।<br>ब्राज़ील की मुद्रा रियाल है, अतः यह युग्म गलत है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ब्राज़ील – पेसो है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000073306","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"The \"Skill India Mission\" aims to empower the youth with relevant skills. Which of the following is a key initiative or program under this mission? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\"स्किल इंडिया मिशन\" का उद्देश्य युवाओं को प्रासंगिक कौशलों से सशक्त बनाना है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा इस मिशन के अंतर्गत एक प्रमुख पहल या कार्यक्रम है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"National Rural Employment Guarantee Scheme (NREGS)","hi":"राष्ट्रीय ग्रामीण रोजगार गारंटी योजना (NREGS)"},"2":{"en":"Startup India Initiative","hi":"स्टार्टअप इंडिया पहल"},"3":{"en":"Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY)","hi":"प्रधानमंत्री कौशल विकास योजना (PMKVY)"},"4":{"en":"Atal Innovation Mission (AIM)","hi":"अटल इनोवेशन मिशन (AIM)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY)</b><br>PMKVY is the flagship scheme of the Skill India Mission, launched in 2015 by the Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship. It provides short-term skill training, assessment and certification to youth along with a monetary reward on successful certification.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Skill India Mission was launched on <b>15 July 2015</b>, observed as World Youth Skills Day, by Prime Minister Narendra Modi.<br>• The Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship (MSDE) was created in <b>2014</b>, separating skill development from the Ministry of Labour.<br>• NREGS (MGNREGA, 2005) is a rural employment guarantee scheme of the Ministry of Rural Development and has no link with skill training.<br>• Startup India was launched on <b>16 January 2016</b>, while the Atal Innovation Mission (Atal Tinkering Labs) is run by <b>NITI Aayog</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – प्रधानमंत्री कौशल विकास योजना (PMKVY)</b><br>PMKVY स्किल इंडिया मिशन की प्रमुख योजना है, जिसे 2015 में कौशल विकास और उद्यमिता मंत्रालय द्वारा आरंभ किया गया। यह युवाओं को अल्पकालिक कौशल प्रशिक्षण, मूल्यांकन तथा प्रमाणन प्रदान करती है और सफल प्रमाणन पर आर्थिक पुरस्कार देती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• स्किल इंडिया मिशन (Skill India Mission) 15 जुलाई 2015 को प्रधानमंत्री नरेंद्र मोदी द्वारा शुरू किया गया; यह दिन विश्व युवा कौशल दिवस (World Youth Skills Day) के रूप में मनाया जाता है।<br>• कौशल विकास और उद्यमिता मंत्रालय (MSDE) का गठन 2014 में किया गया था।<br>• NREGS (मनरेगा, 2005) ग्रामीण विकास मंत्रालय की ग्रामीण रोजगार गारंटी योजना है, जिसका कौशल प्रशिक्षण से कोई संबंध नहीं है।<br>• स्टार्टअप इंडिया (Startup India) 16 जनवरी 2016 को शुरू हुआ तथा अटल इनोवेशन मिशन (Atal Innovation Mission) नीति आयोग द्वारा संचालित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000073307","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"The \"National Food Security Act (NFSA), 2013\" has a primary objective related to food and nutrition. Which of the following best describes this objective? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\"राष्ट्रीय खाद्य सुरक्षा अधिनियम (NFSA), 2013\" का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य खाद्य एवं पोषण से संबंधित है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा इस उद्देश्य का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To promote organic farming practices across the country.","hi":"देश भर में जैविक खेती पद्धतियों को बढ़ावा देना।"},"2":{"en":"To ensure foodgrain procurement at Minimum Support Price (MSP) for all crops.","hi":"सभी फसलों के लिए न्यूनतम समर्थन मूल्य (MSP) पर खाद्यान्न खरीद सुनिश्चित करना।"},"3":{"en":"To provide subsidized foodgrains to a significant proportion of the population.","hi":"जनसंख्या के एक महत्वपूर्ण भाग को सब्सिडी वाला खाद्यान्न उपलब्ध कराना।"},"4":{"en":"To encourage the export of surplus foodgrains to boost the agricultural economy.","hi":"कृषि अर्थव्यवस्था को बढ़ावा देने के लिए अधिशेष खाद्यान्न के निर्यात को प्रोत्साहित करना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – To provide subsidized foodgrains to a significant proportion of the population.</b><br>The NFSA, 2013 adopts a rights-based approach to food security and legally entitles a large share of the population to receive subsidized foodgrains every month through the Public Distribution System. It covers up to 75% of the rural and 50% of the urban population, that is, about two-thirds of the country.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Act was passed in <b>2013</b> and came into force on <b>5 July 2014</b>; it provides 5 kg of foodgrains per person per month at <b>₹3 (rice), ₹2 (wheat) and ₹1 (coarse grains)</b>.<br>• Priority households get 5 kg per person per month, while Antyodaya Anna Yojana families get <b>35 kg per family per month</b>.<br>• The eldest woman of the household aged 18 years or above is the head of the household for issuing ration cards.<br>• MSP procurement is handled by the FCI under the Ministry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution, not by the NFSA.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जनसंख्या के एक महत्वपूर्ण भाग को सब्सिडी वाला खाद्यान्न उपलब्ध कराना।</b><br>NFSA, 2013 खाद्य सुरक्षा के लिए अधिकार-आधारित दृष्टिकोण अपनाता है और जनसंख्या के बड़े भाग को सार्वजनिक वितरण प्रणाली के माध्यम से प्रतिमाह सब्सिडी वाला खाद्यान्न पाने का कानूनी अधिकार देता है। यह ग्रामीण जनसंख्या के 75% तक तथा शहरी जनसंख्या के 50% तक, अर्थात् देश की लगभग दो-तिहाई जनसंख्या को सम्मिलित करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह अधिनियम 2013 में पारित हुआ और 5 जुलाई 2014 से प्रभावी हुआ; इसमें प्रति व्यक्ति प्रतिमाह 5 किग्रा खाद्यान्न चावल ₹3, गेहूँ ₹2 तथा मोटे अनाज ₹1 प्रति किग्रा पर दिया जाता है।<br>• प्राथमिकता वाले परिवारों को प्रति व्यक्ति प्रतिमाह 5 किग्रा तथा अंत्योदय अन्न योजना के परिवारों को प्रति परिवार प्रतिमाह 35 किग्रा मिलता है।<br>• राशन कार्ड जारी करने के लिए 18 वर्ष या अधिक आयु की परिवार की सबसे वयस्क महिला को परिवार का मुखिया माना जाता है।<br>• MSP पर खरीद उपभोक्ता मामले, खाद्य एवं सार्वजनिक वितरण मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत FCI द्वारा की जाती है, NFSA द्वारा नहीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000073308","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"BFI, the governing body for basketball in India, organizes which national-level championship annually? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में बास्केटबॉल की शासी संस्था BFI, प्रतिवर्ष कौन-सी राष्ट्रीय स्तर की चैंपियनशिप आयोजित करती है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"India Slam League","hi":"इंडिया स्लैम लीग"},"2":{"en":"National Club Basketball Cup","hi":"नेशनल क्लब बास्केटबॉल कप"},"3":{"en":"National Basketball Championship","hi":"नेशनल बास्केटबॉल चैंपियनशिप"},"4":{"en":"National Dribble League","hi":"नेशनल ड्रिबल लीग"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – National Basketball Championship</b><br>The Basketball Federation of India (BFI) is the apex body for basketball in India and conducts the National Basketball Championship for men and women every year, in which teams of all states and union territories take part. The other three names are not BFI championships.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Basketball was invented by <b>James Naismith</b> in <b>1891</b> at Springfield, Massachusetts (USA).<br>• The international federation <b>FIBA</b> was founded in 1932 and is headquartered at Mies, Switzerland; basketball became an Olympic sport at <b>Berlin 1936</b>.<br>• The BFI was founded in <b>1935</b>, is affiliated to FIBA, and conducts the National Basketball Championship as its flagship domestic event.<br>• A basketball team has <b>5 players</b> on the court and the standard court measures 28 m × 15 m.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – नेशनल बास्केटबॉल चैंपियनशिप</b><br>भारतीय बास्केटबॉल महासंघ (BFI) भारत में बास्केटबॉल की सर्वोच्च संस्था है और प्रतिवर्ष पुरुषों तथा महिलाओं के लिए नेशनल बास्केटबॉल चैंपियनशिप आयोजित करता है, जिसमें सभी राज्यों व केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों की टीमें भाग लेती हैं। शेष तीन नाम BFI की चैंपियनशिप नहीं हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बास्केटबॉल का आविष्कार जेम्स नाइस्मिथ (James Naismith) ने 1891 में स्प्रिंगफील्ड, मैसाचुसेट्स (अमेरिका) में किया।<br>• अंतर्राष्ट्रीय महासंघ FIBA की स्थापना 1932 में हुई; इसका मुख्यालय मीज़, स्विट्ज़रलैंड में है; बास्केटबॉल बर्लिन ओलंपिक 1936 से ओलंपिक खेल बना।<br>• BFI की स्थापना 1935 में हुई; यह FIBA से संबद्ध है तथा राष्ट्रीय बास्केटबॉल चैंपियनशिप इसका प्रमुख घरेलू आयोजन है।<br>• बास्केटबॉल की एक टीम में 5 खिलाड़ी होते हैं और मानक कोर्ट 28 मीटर × 15 मीटर का होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000073309","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Where did the conclusive match of the <b>2016 Kabaddi World Cup</b> take place? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"<b>2016 कबड्डी विश्व कप</b> का निर्णायक मैच कहाँ हुआ था? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ahmedabad","hi":"अहमदाबाद"},"2":{"en":"Mumbai","hi":"मुंबई"},"3":{"en":"Patna","hi":"पटना"},"4":{"en":"Jaipur","hi":"जयपुर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Ahmedabad</b><br>The final of the 2016 Kabaddi World Cup was played at the Arena by TransStadia in Ahmedabad, Gujarat, where India defeated Iran 38–29 to win the title. In the same tournament Ahmedabad hosted all the matches.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India beat Iran in the finals of all three editions of the standard-style Kabaddi World Cup — <b>2004, 2007 and 2016</b>.<br>• The Indian team in the 2016 final was captained by <b>Anup Kumar</b>, while Iran was led by Meraj Sheykh.<br>• The Kabaddi World Cup is organised by the <b>International Kabaddi Federation (IKF)</b>, whose headquarters is in Jaipur, India.<br>• Kabaddi became a medal sport at the Asian Games in <b>1990 (Beijing)</b>, and India won gold in every edition until 2018.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अहमदाबाद</b><br>2016 कबड्डी विश्व कप का फाइनल गुजरात के अहमदाबाद स्थित एरिना बाय ट्रांसस्टेडिया में खेला गया, जिसमें भारत ने ईरान को 38–29 से हराकर खिताब जीता। इस टूर्नामेंट के सभी मैच अहमदाबाद में ही हुए थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मानक शैली के कबड्डी विश्व कप के तीनों संस्करणों — 2004, 2007 और 2016 — के फाइनल में भारत ने ईरान को हराया।<br>• 2016 के फाइनल में भारतीय टीम के कप्तान अनूप कुमार तथा ईरानी टीम के कप्तान मेराज शेख थे।<br>• कबड्डी विश्व कप का आयोजन अंतर्राष्ट्रीय कबड्डी महासंघ (IKF) करता है, जिसका मुख्यालय जयपुर, भारत में है।<br>• कबड्डी 1990 (बीजिंग) से एशियाई खेलों में पदक खेल बना और 2018 तक हर संस्करण में भारत ने स्वर्ण जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000073310","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"In the Third Five-Year Plan, which trade policy approach was primarily adopted to enhance the nation’s foreign exchange earnings? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"तीसरी पंचवर्षीय योजना में, राष्ट्र की विदेशी मुद्रा आय बढ़ाने के लिए मुख्य रूप से कौन-सा व्यापार नीति दृष्टिकोण अपनाया गया था? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Promotion of import-intensive industries","hi":"आयात-गहन उद्योगों को बढ़ावा"},"2":{"en":"Trade liberalization","hi":"व्यापार उदारीकरण"},"3":{"en":"Implementation of currency devaluation measures","hi":"मुद्रा अवमूल्यन उपायों का क्रियान्वयन"},"4":{"en":"Export promotion","hi":"निर्यात प्रोत्साहन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Export promotion</b><br>The Third Five-Year Plan (1961–66) shifted trade policy towards <b>export promotion</b> to earn the foreign exchange needed for heavy industry and machinery imports. Export incentives, duty drawbacks and import entitlement schemes for exporters were expanded in this period.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Third Plan (1961–66) was based on the <b>Gadgil Plan</b> and aimed at a self-reliant, self-generating economy; its growth target was 5.6%.<br>• It failed mainly because of the <b>1962 (China) and 1965 (Pakistan) wars</b> and the severe drought of 1965–66.<br>• The First Plan (1951–56) rested on the Harrod–Domar model and the Second Plan (1956–61) on the <b>Mahalanobis model</b>, which stressed heavy industry.<br>• The Second Plan was tied to the <b>Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956</b>, which divided industries into Schedule A, B and C.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – निर्यात प्रोत्साहन</b><br>तीसरी पंचवर्षीय योजना (1961–66) में भारी उद्योग तथा मशीनरी के आयात हेतु आवश्यक विदेशी मुद्रा अर्जित करने के लिए व्यापार नीति को निर्यात प्रोत्साहन की ओर मोड़ा गया। इस अवधि में निर्यातकों के लिए निर्यात प्रोत्साहन, शुल्क वापसी तथा आयात अधिकार योजनाएँ विस्तारित की गईं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तीसरी योजना (1961–66) गाडगिल योजना (Gadgil Plan) पर आधारित थी और आत्मनिर्भर अर्थव्यवस्था का लक्ष्य रखती थी; इसका वृद्धि लक्ष्य 5.6% था।<br>• यह योजना मुख्यतः 1962 (चीन) व 1965 (पाकिस्तान) के युद्धों तथा 1965–66 के भीषण सूखे के कारण असफल रही।<br>• प्रथम योजना (1951–56) हैरोड–डोमर मॉडल पर तथा द्वितीय योजना (1956–61) महालनोबिस मॉडल (Mahalanobis model) पर आधारित थी, जिसमें भारी उद्योग पर बल दिया गया।<br>• द्वितीय योजना औद्योगिक नीति प्रस्ताव 1956 (Industrial Policy Resolution 1956) से जुड़ी थी, जिसमें उद्योगों को अनुसूची A, B और C में बाँटा गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000073311","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"Which of the following changes the <b>Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam (BSA)</b>, introduced in relation to electronic evidence, compared to the Indian Evidence Act? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम की तुलना में, <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम (BSA)</b> ने इलेक्ट्रॉनिक साक्ष्य के संबंध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा परिवर्तन किया है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rejects metadata as hearsay","hi":"मेटाडेटा को सुनी-सुनाई बात (hearsay) के रूप में अस्वीकार करता है"},"2":{"en":"Recognizes electronic records as equivalent to oral statements","hi":"इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेखों को मौखिक कथनों के समतुल्य मान्यता देता है"},"3":{"en":"Only printed emails are admissible","hi":"केवल मुद्रित ई-मेल ही ग्राह्य हैं"},"4":{"en":"Broadens scope to include blockchain, cloud logs, and forensic audit trails","hi":"ब्लॉकचेन, क्लाउड लॉग तथा फोरेंसिक ऑडिट ट्रेल्स को सम्मिलित करने के लिए दायरा बढ़ाता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Broadens scope to include blockchain, cloud logs, and forensic audit trails</b><br>The Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023 defines \"electronic record\" very widely, so that any data, metadata, blockchain entry, cloud log or forensic audit trail generated by a computer or communication device is admissible. Thus digital evidence is no longer limited to e-mails and printouts as under the old Act.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The BSA, 2023 replaced the <b>Indian Evidence Act, 1872</b> and has <b>170 sections</b>; the three new criminal laws came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>.<br>• The admissibility certificate for electronic evidence is now given under <b>Section 63 of the BSA</b> (earlier Section 65B of the Indian Evidence Act).<br>• The BSA is read with the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b> (358 sections, replacing the IPC 1860) and the <b>Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023</b> (531 sections, replacing the CrPC 1973).<br>• Electronic records include data in any form such as text, image, audio, video, and information stored in a computer resource or communication device.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – ब्लॉकचेन, क्लाउड लॉग तथा फोरेंसिक ऑडिट ट्रेल्स को सम्मिलित करने के लिए दायरा बढ़ाता है</b><br>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023 \"इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेख\" को अत्यंत व्यापक रूप में परिभाषित करता है, जिससे कंप्यूटर या संचार उपकरण से उत्पन्न कोई भी डेटा, मेटाडेटा, ब्लॉकचेन प्रविष्टि, क्लाउड लॉग अथवा फोरेंसिक ऑडिट ट्रेल ग्राह्य हो जाता है। इस प्रकार डिजिटल साक्ष्य पुराने अधिनियम की तरह केवल ई-मेल व प्रिंटआउट तक सीमित नहीं रहा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023 (BSA) ने भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872 का स्थान लिया; इसमें 170 धाराएँ हैं तथा तीनों नए आपराधिक कानून 1 जुलाई 2024 से प्रभावी हुए।<br>• इलेक्ट्रॉनिक साक्ष्य के लिए प्रमाणन (certificate) अब BSA की धारा 63 के अंतर्गत दिया जाता है (पूर्व में भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम की धारा 65B)।<br>• BSA को भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 (BNS, 358 धाराएँ — IPC 1860 का स्थान) तथा भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 (BNSS, 531 धाराएँ — CrPC 1973 का स्थान) के साथ पढ़ा जाता है।<br>• इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेख में पाठ, चित्र, ऑडियो, वीडियो तथा कंप्यूटर संसाधन या संचार उपकरण में संचित कोई भी सूचना सम्मिलित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000073312","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"As of May 2025, the Vice Chairperson of NITI Aayog and Chairman of the Economic Advisory Council to the Prime Minister (EAC-PM) is ______. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मई 2025 तक, नीति आयोग के उपाध्यक्ष तथा प्रधानमंत्री की आर्थिक सलाहकार परिषद (EAC-PM) के अध्यक्ष ______ हैं। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Suman Bery","hi":"सुमन बेरी"},"2":{"en":"Bibek Debroy","hi":"बिबेक देबरॉय"},"3":{"en":"Rajiv Kumar","hi":"राजीव कुमार"},"4":{"en":"Arvind Panagariya","hi":"अरविंद पनगढ़िया"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Suman Bery</b><br>Suman Bery is the Vice Chairperson of NITI Aayog and holds the additional charge of Chairman of the Economic Advisory Council to the Prime Minister (EAC-PM). He was given the EAC-PM charge after the death of Bibek Debroy on 1 November 2024.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NITI Aayog was formed on <b>1 January 2015</b> by a Cabinet resolution, replacing the Planning Commission; the <b>Prime Minister is its Chairperson</b>.<br>• Suman Bery was appointed Vice Chairperson of NITI Aayog in <b>2022</b>, succeeding Rajiv Kumar; he is a former Director-General of the National Council of Applied Economic Research (NCAER).<br>• Arvind Panagariya was the <b>first Vice Chairperson</b> of NITI Aayog (2015–2017), while Rajiv Kumar held the post from 2017 to 2022.<br>• The EAC-PM is a <b>non-constitutional and non-statutory</b> body that advises the Prime Minister on economic matters.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – सुमन बेरी</b><br>सुमन बेरी नीति आयोग के उपाध्यक्ष हैं तथा प्रधानमंत्री की आर्थिक सलाहकार परिषद (EAC-PM) के अध्यक्ष का अतिरिक्त प्रभार भी संभालते हैं। बिबेक देबरॉय के 1 नवंबर 2024 को निधन के बाद उन्हें यह प्रभार दिया गया था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नीति आयोग की स्थापना 1 जनवरी 2015 को कैबिनेट संकल्प द्वारा हुई, जिसने योजना आयोग का स्थान लिया; प्रधानमंत्री इसके अध्यक्ष होते हैं।<br>• सुमन बेरी 2022 में राजीव कुमार के स्थान पर नीति आयोग के उपाध्यक्ष नियुक्त हुए; वे राष्ट्रीय अनुप्रयुक्त आर्थिक अनुसंधान परिषद (NCAER) के पूर्व महानिदेशक रहे हैं।<br>• अरविंद पनगढ़िया नीति आयोग के प्रथम उपाध्यक्ष (2015–2017) थे, जबकि राजीव कुमार 2017 से 2022 तक इस पद पर रहे।<br>• EAC-PM एक गैर-संवैधानिक एवं गैर-सांविधिक (non-constitutional and non-statutory) निकाय है जो प्रधानमंत्री को आर्थिक विषयों पर सलाह देता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000073313","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Vedic Age","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs is INCORRECTLY matched about the four Vedas? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चार वेदों के संबंध में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा युग्म गलत सुमेलित है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rigveda - Hymns of praise","hi":"ऋग्वेद - स्तुति के मंत्र"},"2":{"en":"Yajurveda - Rituals and sacrificial prayers","hi":"यजुर्वेद - कर्मकांड और यज्ञीय प्रार्थनाएँ"},"3":{"en":"Samaveda - Philosophical teachings","hi":"सामवेद - दार्शनिक शिक्षाएँ"},"4":{"en":"Atharvaveda - Spells to ward off evils and diseases","hi":"अथर्ववेद - रोगों और अनिष्टों को दूर करने के मंत्र"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Samaveda - Philosophical teachings</b><br>The Samaveda is the <b>Veda of melodies and chants</b>; it contains verses meant to be sung by the udgatri priest during sacrifices and is regarded as the origin of Indian music. Philosophical teachings are found in the Upanishads and Aranyakas, not in the Samaveda, so this pair is wrongly matched.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Rigveda is the <b>oldest Veda</b>, with 10 mandalas and 1028 hymns; it contains the Gayatri Mantra and the Purusha Sukta.<br>• The Yajurveda deals with <b>sacrificial formulae and rituals</b> and has two branches — Shukla (white) and Krishna (black) Yajurveda.<br>• The Atharvaveda contains <b>charms, spells and medicines</b> against disease and evil, and is also called Brahmaveda.<br>• The word \"Veda\" means knowledge; the four Vedas are Rigveda, Samaveda, Yajurveda and Atharvaveda, while the Upanishads are called Vedanta.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सामवेद - दार्शनिक शिक्षाएँ</b><br>सामवेद <b>धुनों और साम-गान का वेद</b> है; इसमें ऐसे मंत्र हैं जो यज्ञ के समय उद्गाता ऋत्विक द्वारा गाए जाते थे और इसे भारतीय संगीत का उद्गम माना जाता है। दार्शनिक शिक्षाएँ उपनिषदों तथा आरण्यकों में मिलती हैं, सामवेद में नहीं; अतः यह युग्म गलत सुमेलित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ऋग्वेद सबसे प्राचीन वेद है, जिसमें 10 मंडल तथा 1028 सूक्त हैं; इसमें गायत्री मंत्र व पुरुष सूक्त हैं।<br>• यजुर्वेद यज्ञीय सूत्रों एवं कर्मकांड से संबंधित है तथा इसकी दो शाखाएँ हैं — शुक्ल (श्वेत) तथा कृष्ण यजुर्वेद।<br>• अथर्ववेद में रोग व अनिष्टों को दूर करने के मंत्र, जादू-टोने एवं औषधियाँ हैं; इसे ब्रह्मवेद (Brahmaveda) भी कहा जाता है।<br>• \"वेद\" का अर्थ ज्ञान है; चार वेद ऋग्वेद, सामवेद, यजुर्वेद और अथर्ववेद हैं, तथा उपनिषदों को वेदांत कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000073314","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which is NOT a major thermal power station in India? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन भारत का प्रमुख ताप विद्युत केंद्र नहीं है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Vijayawada","hi":"विजयवाड़ा"},"2":{"en":"Nashik","hi":"नासिक"},"3":{"en":"Sabarmati","hi":"साबरमती"},"4":{"en":"Tarapur","hi":"तारापुर"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Tarapur</b><br>Tarapur, in Palghar district of Maharashtra, is a <b>nuclear power station</b> and not a thermal one. Vijayawada (Dr. Narla Tata Rao Thermal Power Station), Nashik and Sabarmati are coal-based thermal power stations, so Tarapur is the odd one out.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Tarapur Atomic Power Station started in <b>1969</b> and was India’s <b>first nuclear power plant</b>; its two boiling water reactors were built with US assistance.<br>• India’s largest thermal power station is <b>Vindhyachal</b> in Singrauli, Madhya Pradesh (4,760 MW).<br>• The Nashik thermal station belongs to Maharashtra and the Sabarmati station is located in Ahmedabad, Gujarat.<br>• Nuclear power plants in India are operated by the <b>NPCIL</b>, while thermal plants are run by NTPC and state power corporations.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – तारापुर</b><br>महाराष्ट्र के पालघर जिले में स्थित तारापुर <b>परमाणु विद्युत केंद्र</b> है, ताप विद्युत केंद्र नहीं। विजयवाड़ा (डॉ. नारला टाटा राव ताप विद्युत केंद्र), नासिक तथा साबरमती कोयला आधारित ताप विद्युत केंद्र हैं, अतः तारापुर अन्य से भिन्न है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तारापुर परमाणु विद्युत केंद्र की शुरुआत 1969 में हुई थी और यह भारत का प्रथम परमाणु विद्युत केंद्र था; इसके दो बॉयलिंग वाटर रिएक्टर अमेरिका के सहयोग से बने थे।<br>• भारत का सबसे बड़ा ताप विद्युत केंद्र मध्य प्रदेश के सिंगरौली स्थित विंध्याचल (Vindhyachal) है, जिसकी क्षमता 4,760 मेगावाट है।<br>• नासिक ताप विद्युत केंद्र महाराष्ट्र में तथा साबरमती केंद्र अहमदाबाद, गुजरात में स्थित है।<br>• भारत में परमाणु विद्युत केंद्र NPCIL द्वारा तथा ताप विद्युत केंद्र NTPC एवं राज्य विद्युत निगमों द्वारा संचालित किए जाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000073315","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Governor-General and Viceroy","question":{"en":"Which of the following was a key feature of the Regulating Act of <b>1773</b>? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी <b>1773</b> के विनियमन अधिनियम की प्रमुख विशेषता थी? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It granted complete autonomy to the East India Company.","hi":"इसने ईस्ट इंडिया कंपनी को पूर्ण स्वायत्तता प्रदान की।"},"2":{"en":"It made the Governor of Bombay the supreme authority in India.","hi":"इसने बॉम्बे के गवर्नर को भारत में सर्वोच्च अधिकारी बना दिया।"},"3":{"en":"It limited the British Parliament’s power over Company affairs.","hi":"इसने कंपनी के मामलों पर ब्रिटिश संसद की शक्ति को सीमित किया।"},"4":{"en":"It introduced Parliamentary supervision over the Company’s administration.","hi":"इसने कंपनी के प्रशासन पर संसदीय निगरानी की शुरुआत की।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – It introduced Parliamentary supervision over the Company’s administration.</b><br>The Regulating Act of 1773 was the first step taken by the British Parliament to control and regulate the East India Company’s affairs, which had become corrupt. It recognised the Company’s political and administrative functions and subjected its governance in India to parliamentary supervision.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It designated the Governor of Bengal as the <b>Governor-General of Bengal</b>; <b>Lord Warren Hastings</b> was the first to hold this post (1773–85).<br>• It established the <b>Supreme Court at Calcutta in 1774</b>, with Sir Elijah Impey as its first Chief Justice.<br>• A Council of four members was created to assist the Governor-General, and the presidencies of Bombay and Madras were subordinated to Bengal.<br>• The Act forbade Company servants from private trade and from accepting presents or bribes, and the Court of Directors had to report revenue, civil and military matters to the British government.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – इसने कंपनी के प्रशासन पर संसदीय निगरानी की शुरुआत की।</b><br>विनियमन अधिनियम 1773 ब्रिटिश संसद द्वारा ईस्ट इंडिया कंपनी के भ्रष्ट हो चुके मामलों को नियंत्रित और विनियमित करने की पहली पहल थी। इसने कंपनी के राजनीतिक एवं प्रशासनिक कार्यों को मान्यता दी तथा भारत में उसके शासन को संसदीय निगरानी के अधीन किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसने बंगाल के गवर्नर को बंगाल का गवर्नर-जनरल पदनाम दिया; लॉर्ड वारेन हेस्टिंग्स इस पद पर नियुक्त प्रथम व्यक्ति थे (1773–85)।<br>• इसने 1774 में कलकत्ता में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की स्थापना की, जिसके प्रथम मुख्य न्यायाधीश सर एलिजा इम्पे थे।<br>• गवर्नर-जनरल की सहायता हेतु चार सदस्यीय परिषद बनाई गई तथा बॉम्बे और मद्रास प्रेसीडेंसी को बंगाल के अधीन किया गया।<br>• इस अधिनियम ने कंपनी कर्मचारियों के निजी व्यापार तथा उपहार/रिश्वत लेने पर रोक लगाई और निदेशक मंडल को ब्रिटिश सरकार को राजस्व, असैनिक व सैन्य विवरण देने का निर्देश दिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000073316","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"According to Article 64 of the Indian Constitution, the Vice-President of India is the ex officio Chairman of the: [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 64 के अनुसार, भारत का उपराष्ट्रपति पदेन सभापति होता है: [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lok Sabha","hi":"लोकसभा"},"2":{"en":"Legislative Assembly","hi":"विधानसभा"},"3":{"en":"Council of States","hi":"राज्यसभा"},"4":{"en":"Council of Ministers","hi":"मंत्रिपरिषद"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Council of States</b><br>Article 64 of the Constitution states that the Vice-President shall be the <b>ex officio Chairman of the Council of States (Rajya Sabha)</b>. He is not a member of either House, but presides over the Rajya Sabha and has only a casting vote in case of a tie.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Article 63 provides that there shall be a Vice-President of India; Article 65 makes him acting President during a vacancy in the office of President.<br>• The Vice-President is elected by an electoral college of the <b>elected and nominated members of both Houses of Parliament</b> (Article 66), by proportional representation by single transferable vote.<br>• He holds office for <b>5 years</b> but can be removed by a resolution passed by an effective majority of the Rajya Sabha and agreed to by the Lok Sabha (Article 67).<br>• The office of the Deputy Chairman of the Rajya Sabha is provided in <b>Article 89</b>, while the Speaker of the Lok Sabha presides over the Lok Sabha under Article 93.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – राज्यसभा</b><br>संविधान का अनुच्छेद 64 कहता है कि उपराष्ट्रपति राज्यसभा (Council of States) का पदेन सभापति होगा। वह किसी भी सदन का सदस्य नहीं होता, परंतु राज्यसभा की अध्यक्षता करता है और मत बराबर होने पर केवल निर्णायक मत दे सकता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अनुच्छेद 63 में उपराष्ट्रपति पद का प्रावधान है; अनुच्छेद 65 के अनुसार राष्ट्रपति के पद में रिक्ति होने पर वह कार्यवाहक राष्ट्रपति बनता है।<br>• उपराष्ट्रपति का निर्वाचन संसद के दोनों सदनों के निर्वाचित एवं नामनिर्देशित सदस्यों के निर्वाचक मंडल द्वारा (अनुच्छेद 66) आनुपातिक प्रतिनिधित्व की एकल संक्रमणीय मत पद्धति से होता है।<br>• उसका कार्यकाल 5 वर्ष का होता है, परंतु राज्यसभा के प्रभावी बहुमत से पारित तथा लोकसभा द्वारा सहमत संकल्प से उसे हटाया जा सकता है (अनुच्छेद 67)।<br>• राज्यसभा के उपसभापति का पद अनुच्छेद 89 में तथा लोकसभा अध्यक्ष की अध्यक्षता अनुच्छेद 93 में दी गई है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000073317","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Magnetic Effect of Electric Current","question":{"en":"What is the SI unit of magnetic flux density? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चुंबकीय फ्लक्स घनत्व का SI मात्रक क्या है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tesla","hi":"टेस्ला"},"2":{"en":"Weber","hi":"वेबर"},"3":{"en":"Henry","hi":"हेनरी"},"4":{"en":"Gauss","hi":"गॉस"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Tesla</b><br>The SI unit of magnetic flux density (B) is the tesla (T), where 1 tesla = 1 weber per square metre (1 T = 1 Wb/m²). It is named after the scientist Nikola Tesla.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Magnetic flux (\\(\\Phi\\)) is measured in <b>weber (Wb)</b>, and its CGS unit is the maxwell.<br>• Inductance is measured in <b>henry (H)</b>, named after Joseph Henry.<br>• The <b>gauss</b> is the CGS unit of magnetic flux density; 1 tesla = \\(10^4\\) gauss.<br>• Magnetic flux density is a vector quantity; the earth’s magnetic field at its surface is about \\(0.5\\) gauss or \\(5 \\times 10^{-5}\\) tesla.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – टेस्ला</b><br>चुंबकीय फ्लक्स घनत्व (B) का SI मात्रक टेस्ला (T) है, जहाँ 1 टेस्ला = 1 वेबर प्रति वर्ग मीटर (1 T = 1 Wb/m²)। यह वैज्ञानिक निकोला टेस्ला के नाम पर है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चुंबकीय फ्लक्स (\\(\\Phi\\)) का मात्रक वेबर (Wb) है तथा इसका CGS मात्रक मैक्सवेल है।<br>• प्रेरकत्व (Inductance) का मात्रक हेनरी (H) है, जो जोसेफ हेनरी के नाम पर है।<br>• गॉस (Gauss) चुंबकीय फ्लक्स घनत्व का CGS मात्रक है; 1 टेस्ला = \\(10^4\\) गॉस।<br>• चुंबकीय फ्लक्स घनत्व सदिश राशि है; पृथ्वी की सतह पर इसका मान लगभग \\(0.5\\) गॉस अर्थात् \\(5 \\times 10^{-5}\\) टेस्ला होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000073318","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian sportsperson is famously known as the \"Payolli Express\"? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस भारतीय खिलाड़ी को \"पायोली एक्सप्रेस\" के नाम से प्रसिद्धि मिली है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hima Das","hi":"हिमा दास"},"2":{"en":"P.T. Usha","hi":"पी.टी. उषा"},"3":{"en":"Anju Bobby George","hi":"अंजू बॉबी जॉर्ज"},"4":{"en":"Shiny Abraham","hi":"शाइनी अब्राहम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – P.T. Usha</b><br>P.T. Usha, born at Payyoli in Kerala, is called the \"Payyoli Express\" for her speed on the track. She is regarded as the \"Queen of Indian Athletics\" and was the first Indian woman to reach an Olympic final.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• P.T. Usha missed the bronze medal in the <b>400 m hurdles at the 1984 Los Angeles Olympics</b> by just one-hundredth of a second and finished fourth.<br>• She won four gold medals and one silver at the <b>1985 Asian Athletics Championships</b> in Jakarta, a record performance.<br>• She was awarded the <b>Padma Shri in 1985</b> and the <b>Padma Bhushan in 2023</b>, and was nominated to the Rajya Sabha in 2022.<br>• She became the <b>first woman President of the Indian Olympic Association</b> in 2022; Hima Das is known as the \"Dhing Express\" of Assam.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पी.टी. उषा</b><br>केरल के पायोली में जन्मी पी.टी. उषा को ट्रैक पर उनकी गति के कारण \"पायोली एक्सप्रेस\" कहा जाता है। उन्हें \"भारतीय एथलेटिक्स की रानी\" माना जाता है और वे ओलंपिक फाइनल में पहुँचने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला थीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पी.टी. उषा 1984 के लॉस एंजिल्स ओलंपिक की 400 मीटर हर्डल्स स्पर्धा में केवल एक-सौवें सेकंड से कांस्य पदक से चूककर चौथे स्थान पर रहीं।<br>• उन्होंने 1985 की जकार्ता एशियाई एथलेटिक्स चैंपियनशिप में चार स्वर्ण तथा एक रजत पदक जीते, जो एक रिकॉर्ड प्रदर्शन था।<br>• उन्हें 1985 में पद्म श्री तथा 2023 में पद्म भूषण से सम्मानित किया गया; 2022 में वे राज्यसभा के लिए नामनिर्देशित हुईं।<br>• वे 2022 में भारतीय ओलंपिक संघ की पहली महिला अध्यक्ष बनीं; हिमा दास को असम की \"ढिंग एक्सप्रेस\" कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000073319","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"What happened to mature Harappan culture after around 1900 BC? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"लगभग 1900 ईसा पूर्व के बाद परिपक्व हड़प्पा संस्कृति का क्या हुआ? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Instant, total extinction","hi":"तात्कालिक, पूर्ण विलोपन"},"2":{"en":"Faded peripheral survival","hi":"क्षीण परिधीय अस्तित्व"},"3":{"en":"Core urban expansion","hi":"मुख्य नगरीय विस्तार"},"4":{"en":"Shift to metal weaponry","hi":"धातु शस्त्रों की ओर परिवर्तन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Faded peripheral survival</b><br>After about <b>1900 BC</b> the mature Harappan cities decayed and the culture passed into the <b>Late Harappan</b> phase. Urban features such as planned streets, drains and seals disappeared, but the culture did not vanish — it survived in a faded, rural and peripheral form in regions like Gujarat, Haryana and eastern Punjab.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Mature Harappan period is dated <b>2600–1900 BCE</b> and the Late Harappan (Cemetery H) phase 1900–1300 BCE.<br>• Decline factors include climatic change, drying of the Ghaggar-Hakra, floods, and the collapse of trade; Mortimer Wheeler’s invasion theory is now rejected.<br>• Important sites: Harappa and Mohenjodaro (Pakistan), <b>Rakhigarhi</b> (largest in India), Dholavira, Lothal (dockyard) and Kalibangan.<br>• Dholavira in Gujarat was declared a <b>UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2021</b>; the Harappans used a script that is still undeciphered.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – क्षीण परिधीय अस्तित्व</b><br>लगभग 1900 ईसा पूर्व के बाद परिपक्व हड़प्पा नगर क्षय हो गए और संस्कृति उत्तर-हड़प्पा काल में प्रवेश कर गई। नियोजित गलियाँ, नालियाँ और मुहरें जैसी नगरीय विशेषताएँ लुप्त हो गईं, परंतु संस्कृति पूर्णतः समाप्त नहीं हुई — गुजरात, हरियाणा व पूर्वी पंजाब जैसे क्षेत्रों में यह क्षीण, ग्रामीण एवं परिधीय रूप में बनी रही।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• परिपक्व हड़प्पा काल 2600–1900 ईसा पूर्व तथा उत्तर-हड़प्पा (Cemetery H) चरण 1900–1300 ईसा पूर्व माना जाता है।<br>• ह्रास के कारणों में जलवायु परिवर्तन, घग्गर-हाकरा का सूखना, बाढ़ तथा व्यापार का पतन सम्मिलित हैं; मॉर्टिमर व्हीलर का आक्रमण सिद्धांत अब मान्य नहीं है।<br>• प्रमुख स्थल: हड़प्पा व मोहनजोदड़ो (पाकिस्तान), राखीगढ़ी (भारत में सबसे बड़ा), धोलावीरा, लोथल (गोदी) तथा कालीबंगा।<br>• गुजरात का धोलावीरा 2021 में यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल घोषित हुआ; हड़प्पा लिपि आज तक अपठित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000073320","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: National Organisations","question":{"en":"Which premier agency, now preparing the uncrewed Gaganyaan flight tests, was headed by S. Somanath as Chairman from 2022 to 2025? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एस. सोमनाथ 2022 से 2025 तक किस प्रमुख एजेंसी के अध्यक्ष रहे, जो अब मानवरहित गगनयान उड़ान परीक्षणों की तैयारी कर रही है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"DRDO (Defence Research and Development Organisation)","hi":"DRDO (रक्षा अनुसंधान एवं विकास संगठन)"},"2":{"en":"ISRO (Indian Space Research Organisation)","hi":"इसरो (भारतीय अंतरिक्ष अनुसंधान संगठन)"},"3":{"en":"BARC (Bhabha Atomic Research Centre)","hi":"BARC (भाभा परमाणु अनुसंधान केंद्र)"},"4":{"en":"CSIR (Council of Scientific and Industrial Research)","hi":"CSIR (वैज्ञानिक एवं औद्योगिक अनुसंधान परिषद)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – ISRO (Indian Space Research Organisation)</b><br>S. Somanath was the Chairman of ISRO from January 2022 to January 2025; he was succeeded by <b>V. Narayanan</b> in January 2025. ISRO runs the Gaganyaan programme, under which uncrewed flight tests of the crew module and crew escape system are being carried out before the crewed mission. ISRO is India’s national space agency, headquartered at Bengaluru.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• ISRO was formed on <b>15 August 1969</b>; its headquarters is at <b>Antariksh Bhavan, Bengaluru</b>.<br>• The Indian space programme began with <b>INCOSPAR (1962)</b>, founded by <b>Vikram Sarabhai</b>, who is called the father of the Indian space programme.<br>• ISRO’s first satellite was <b>Aryabhata (1975)</b>; Chandrayaan-3 landed near the lunar south pole on <b>23 August 2023</b>, making India the first country to do so.<br>• Gaganyaan aims to send a <b>three-member crew</b> into a low earth orbit of about 400 km; DRDO works on defence technology, BARC on nuclear research and CSIR on scientific research.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – इसरो (भारतीय अंतरिक्ष अनुसंधान संगठन)</b><br>एस. सोमनाथ जनवरी 2022 से जनवरी 2025 तक इसरो के अध्यक्ष रहे; जनवरी 2025 में <b>वी. नारायणन</b> ने उनका स्थान लिया। इसरो गगनयान कार्यक्रम चलाता है, जिसके अंतर्गत मानव मिशन से पहले क्रू मॉड्यूल व क्रू एस्केप सिस्टम के मानवरहित उड़ान परीक्षण किए जा रहे हैं। इसरो भारत की राष्ट्रीय अंतरिक्ष एजेंसी है, जिसका मुख्यालय बेंगलुरु में है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसरो की स्थापना 15 अगस्त 1969 को हुई; इसका मुख्यालय अंतरिक्ष भवन, बेंगलुरु में है।<br>• भारतीय अंतरिक्ष कार्यक्रम की शुरुआत INCOSPAR (1962) से हुई, जिसकी स्थापना विक्रम साराभाई ने की; उन्हें भारतीय अंतरिक्ष कार्यक्रम का जनक कहा जाता है।<br>• इसरो का प्रथम उपग्रह आर्यभट (1975) था; चंद्रयान-3 ने 23 अगस्त 2023 को चंद्रमा के दक्षिणी ध्रुव के निकट उतरकर भारत को ऐसा करने वाला पहला देश बनाया।<br>• गगनयान का लक्ष्य तीन सदस्यीय दल को लगभग 400 किमी की निम्न पृथ्वी कक्षा में भेजना है; DRDO रक्षा तकनीक, BARC परमाणु अनुसंधान तथा CSIR वैज्ञानिक अनुसंधान पर कार्य करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000073321","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Rocks, Continents, and Oceans","question":{"en":"The Mozambique Channel is located between which two places? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मोज़ाम्बिक चैनल किन दो स्थानों के बीच स्थित है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Madagascar and Mozambique","hi":"मेडागास्कर और मोज़ाम्बिक"},"2":{"en":"Indonesia and Malaysia","hi":"इंडोनेशिया और मलेशिया"},"3":{"en":"Oman and Iran","hi":"ओमान और ईरान"},"4":{"en":"India and Sri Lanka","hi":"भारत और श्रीलंका"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Madagascar and Mozambique</b><br>The Mozambique Channel is a part of the <b>Indian Ocean</b> that separates the island of Madagascar from the mainland country of Mozambique in south-eastern Africa. It links the northern Indian Ocean with the waters off South Africa.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The channel is about <b>1,600 km long</b> and its width varies between roughly 400 km and 950 km.<br>• Madagascar is the <b>fourth largest island</b> in the world, and the Mozambique Channel carries the warm Agulhas Current southwards.<br>• Strait of Malacca lies between Malaysia and Indonesia (Sumatra), the Strait of Hormuz between Oman and Iran, and the <b>Palk Strait</b> between India and Sri Lanka.<br>• The capital of Mozambique is <b>Maputo</b>, while Madagascar’s capital is Antananarivo.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मेडागास्कर और मोज़ाम्बिक</b><br>मोज़ाम्बिक चैनल हिंद महासागर का वह भाग है जो मेडागास्कर द्वीप को दक्षिण-पूर्वी अफ्रीका के मुख्य भूभाग मोज़ाम्बिक से अलग करता है। यह उत्तरी हिंद महासागर को दक्षिण अफ्रीका के निकटवर्ती जल से जोड़ता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह चैनल लगभग 1,600 किमी लंबा है तथा इसकी चौड़ाई लगभग 400 किमी से 950 किमी के बीच है।<br>• मेडागास्कर विश्व का चौथा सबसे बड़ा द्वीप है; मोज़ाम्बिक चैनल से गर्म अगुल्हास धारा (Agulhas Current) दक्षिण की ओर बहती है।<br>• मलक्का जलडमरूमध्य मलेशिया व इंडोनेशिया (सुमात्रा), हॉर्मुज जलडमरूमध्य ओमान व ईरान तथा पाक जलडमरूमध्य (Palk Strait) भारत व श्रीलंका के बीच है।<br>• मोज़ाम्बिक की राजधानी मापुतो तथा मेडागास्कर की राजधानी अंतानानारिवो है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000073322","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A police officer receives a warrant to arrest \"R\". After conducting a reasonable inquiry and acting in good faith, he arrests S, believing S to be R. Later it is discovered that S was entirely innocent, and the warrant never applied to him. Which of the following is the most accurate legal position under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक पुलिस अधिकारी को \"R\" को गिरफ्तार करने का वारंट प्राप्त होता है। उचित जाँच करने तथा सद्भावना से कार्य करने के बाद वह S को R मानकर गिरफ्तार कर लेता है। बाद में पता चलता है कि S पूर्णतः निर्दोष था और वारंट उस पर कभी लागू ही नहीं होता था। भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत भारत में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी विधिक स्थिति सर्वाधिक सटीक है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The officer is liable because wrongful arrest always constitutes an offence.","hi":"अधिकारी उत्तरदायी है, क्योंकि गलत गिरफ्तारी सदैव अपराध होती है।"},"2":{"en":"The officer is protected only if the court issuing the warrant has jurisdiction.","hi":"अधिकारी केवल तभी संरक्षित है जब वारंट जारी करने वाले न्यायालय का अधिकारक्षेत्र हो।"},"3":{"en":"The officer is protected because of a mistake of fact made in good faith.","hi":"अधिकारी संरक्षित है, क्योंकि यह सद्भावना में की गई तथ्य की त्रुटि थी।"},"4":{"en":"The officer is liable because identity mistakes are mistakes of law.","hi":"अधिकारी उत्तरदायी है, क्योंकि पहचान की त्रुटियाँ विधि की त्रुटियाँ होती हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The officer is protected because of a mistake of fact made in good faith.</b><br>The BNS, 2023 gives a general exception for acts done by a person who, by reason of a <b>mistake of fact and not of law, in good faith</b>, believes himself to be bound or justified by law to do the act. Identifying S as R after a reasonable inquiry is a mistake of fact in good faith, so the officer’s arrest is not an offence.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The protection follows the old <b>Sections 76 and 79 of the IPC, 1860</b>, now carried into the general exceptions of the BNS, 2023.<br>• A mistake of <b>fact</b> (a wrong belief about circumstances) excuses the act, but a mistake of <b>law</b> (ignorance of the legal rule) does not.<br>• \"Good faith\" under the BNS means an act done with <b>due care and attention</b>; a hasty or mala fide arrest gets no protection.<br>• Procedure for arrest is now governed by the <b>BNSS, 2023</b>, which requires the grounds of arrest to be communicated and, in many cases, a written notice of appearance instead of immediate arrest.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अधिकारी संरक्षित है, क्योंकि यह सद्भावना में की गई तथ्य की त्रुटि थी।</b><br>BNS, 2023 में उस व्यक्ति के कार्य के लिए सामान्य अपवाद दिया गया है जो तथ्य की त्रुटि (विधि की नहीं) के कारण, सद्भावना से यह मानता है कि वह उस कार्य को करने के लिए विधि द्वारा बाध्य या अधिकृत है। उचित जाँच के बाद S को R मानना सद्भावना में तथ्य की त्रुटि है, अतः अधिकारी की गिरफ्तारी अपराध नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह संरक्षण पुराने IPC, 1860 की धारा 76 व 79 का अनुसरण करता है, जिसे BNS, 2023 के सामान्य अपवादों (General Exceptions) में सम्मिलित किया गया है।<br>• तथ्य की त्रुटि (परिस्थितियों के बारे में गलत धारणा) कार्य को क्षम्य बनाती है, परंतु विधि की त्रुटि (विधिक नियम का अज्ञान) नहीं।<br>• BNS में \"सद्भावना\" (Good faith) का अर्थ उचित सावधानी एवं ध्यान से किया गया कार्य है; जल्दबाजी या दुर्भावना से की गई गिरफ्तारी को संरक्षण नहीं मिलता।<br>• गिरफ्तारी की प्रक्रिया अब BNSS, 2023 से नियंत्रित होती है, जिसमें गिरफ्तारी के आधार बताना तथा अनेक मामलों में तत्काल गिरफ्तारी के स्थान पर उपस्थिति का लिखित नोटिस देना आवश्यक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000073323","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Part 1 and Part 2 of the Constitution","question":{"en":"The concept of a \"Union of States\" under Article 1 of the Constitution of India implies that: [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के संविधान के अनुच्छेद 1 के अंतर्गत \"राज्यों के संघ\" की संकल्पना का अर्थ है कि: [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"States possess a constitutional right to secede","hi":"राज्यों को अलग होने का संवैधानिक अधिकार प्राप्त है"},"2":{"en":"The Indian federation originated through agreement among sovereign states.","hi":"भारतीय संघ का उद्भव संप्रभु राज्यों के बीच समझौते से हुआ।"},"3":{"en":"The Union is indestructible, though States may be reorganized.","hi":"संघ अविनाशी है, हालाँकि राज्यों का पुनर्गठन किया जा सकता है।"},"4":{"en":"States have equal sovereignty with the union.","hi":"राज्यों को संघ के समान ही संप्रभुता प्राप्त है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The Union is indestructible, though States may be reorganized.</b><br>Article 1 declares that \"India, that is Bharat, shall be a Union of States\". Dr. B.R. Ambedkar explained that the word \"Union\" was deliberately used to show that (i) the federation is not the result of an agreement among states and (ii) no state has the right to secede, so the Union is indestructible, although Parliament may reorganize states.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Article 1 describes India as a <b>Union of States</b> and says the territory of India includes states, union territories and any territory acquired.<br>• Under <b>Article 3</b>, Parliament can form new states, alter boundaries or names of states by a <b>simple majority</b>, with the President referring the bill to the state legislature for its views.<br>• Article 2 empowers Parliament to admit or establish new states.<br>• India is called a <b>\"quasi-federal\"</b> state (K.C. Wheare) because of a strong Centre, single citizenship and the appointment of governors by the President.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – संघ अविनाशी है, हालाँकि राज्यों का पुनर्गठन किया जा सकता है।</b><br>अनुच्छेद 1 घोषित करता है कि \"भारत, अर्थात् इंडिया, राज्यों का संघ होगा\"। डॉ. भीमराव आंबेडकर ने बताया कि \"संघ\" (Union) शब्द जानबूझकर इसलिए प्रयुक्त हुआ कि (i) यह संघ राज्यों के समझौते का परिणाम नहीं है और (ii) किसी राज्य को अलग होने का अधिकार नहीं है; अतः संघ अविनाशी है, यद्यपि संसद राज्यों का पुनर्गठन कर सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अनुच्छेद 1 भारत को राज्यों का संघ कहता है तथा भारत के राज्यक्षेत्र में राज्य, केंद्रशासित प्रदेश और अर्जित क्षेत्र सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• अनुच्छेद 3 के अंतर्गत संसद साधारण बहुमत से नए राज्य बना सकती है, सीमाओं या नामों में परिवर्तन कर सकती है, जिसमें विधेयक पर राज्य विधानमंडल की राय हेतु राष्ट्रपति उसे भेजता है।<br>• अनुच्छेद 2 संसद को नए राज्यों के प्रवेश या स्थापना की शक्ति देता है।<br>• मजबूत केंद्र, एकल नागरिकता तथा राष्ट्रपति द्वारा राज्यपाल की नियुक्ति के कारण भारत को \"अर्ध-संघीय\" (quasi-federal) राज्य कहा जाता है (के.सी. व्हीयर)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000073324","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"The economic reforms initiated in 1991 promoted which of the following policy combinations? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 में आरंभ किए गए आर्थिक सुधारों ने निम्नलिखित में से किस नीतिगत संयोजन को बढ़ावा दिया? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Industrial licensing and import restrictions","hi":"औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग और आयात प्रतिबंध"},"2":{"en":"Market based pricing and industrial dereservation","hi":"बाजार आधारित मूल्य निर्धारण और औद्योगिक डी-आरक्षण"},"3":{"en":"Public ownership and centralised price fixation","hi":"सार्वजनिक स्वामित्व और केंद्रीकृत मूल्य निर्धारण"},"4":{"en":"Export controls and mandatory production quotas","hi":"निर्यात नियंत्रण और अनिवार्य उत्पादन कोटा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Market based pricing and industrial dereservation</b><br>The 1991 reforms introduced Liberalisation, Privatisation and Globalisation (LPG). Prices were increasingly left to market forces, industrial licensing was abolished for most industries, and several sectors reserved for the public sector were de-reserved and opened to private and foreign investment.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The reforms started in <b>July 1991</b> under Prime Minister <b>P.V. Narasimha Rao</b> and Finance Minister <b>Dr. Manmohan Singh</b>.<br>• The <b>New Industrial Policy, 1991</b> abolished industrial licensing except for a small list of industries and reduced the number of industries reserved for the public sector from 17 to 8 (later 2).<br>• The rupee was devalued in two steps in <b>July 1991</b>, and the MRTP Act limits on large houses were relaxed.<br>• The immediate trigger was a balance of payments crisis, when foreign exchange reserves fell to about <b>1 billion US dollars</b> — enough for barely two weeks of imports.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बाजार आधारित मूल्य निर्धारण और औद्योगिक डी-आरक्षण</b><br>1991 के सुधारों ने उदारीकरण, निजीकरण एवं वैश्वीकरण (LPG) को लागू किया। कीमतें उत्तरोत्तर बाजार शक्तियों पर छोड़ी गईं, अधिकांश उद्योगों के लिए औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग समाप्त की गई तथा सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र हेतु आरक्षित अनेक क्षेत्रों को डी-आरक्षित कर निजी व विदेशी निवेश के लिए खोला गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सुधार जुलाई 1991 में प्रधानमंत्री पी.वी. नरसिम्हा राव तथा वित्त मंत्री डॉ. मनमोहन सिंह के नेतृत्व में आरंभ हुए।<br>• नई औद्योगिक नीति, 1991 ने कुछ उद्योगों को छोड़कर औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग समाप्त की तथा सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र हेतु आरक्षित उद्योगों की संख्या 17 से घटाकर 8 (बाद में 2) कर दी।<br>• जुलाई 1991 में रुपये का दो चरणों में अवमूल्यन किया गया तथा बड़े औद्योगिक घरानों पर MRTP अधिनियम की सीमाएँ शिथिल की गईं।<br>• सुधारों का तात्कालिक कारण भुगतान संतुलन संकट था, जब विदेशी मुद्रा भंडार लगभग 1 अरब डॉलर रह गया था — जो मुश्किल से दो सप्ताह के आयात के लिए पर्याप्त था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000073325","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"India approached which institution for financial assistance during the 1991 economic crisis? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक संकट के दौरान भारत ने किस संस्था से वित्तीय सहायता मांगी? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"World Trade Organisation","hi":"विश्व व्यापार संगठन"},"2":{"en":"European Central Bank","hi":"यूरोपीय केंद्रीय बैंक"},"3":{"en":"International Monetary Fund","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष"},"4":{"en":"Asian Development Bank","hi":"एशियाई विकास बैंक"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – International Monetary Fund</b><br>In 1991 India approached the <b>International Monetary Fund (IMF)</b> for a standby arrangement and later the Extended Fund Facility, and also borrowed from the World Bank. The loans were given with conditions of devaluation, fiscal deficit reduction and trade liberalisation, which shaped the LPG reforms.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The IMF was set up at the <b>Bretton Woods Conference (1944)</b> and began work in 1945; its headquarters is in <b>Washington D.C.</b><br>• The IMF gives short-term loans to correct balance of payments problems, while the World Bank funds long-term development projects.<br>• The <b>WTO</b> was established in <b>1995</b> with headquarters at Geneva, the <b>ADB</b> in 1966 at Manila, and the ECB in 1998 at Frankfurt.<br>• To raise funds during the crisis, India pledged part of its gold reserves to the Bank of England in 1991.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष</b><br>1991 में भारत ने स्टैंडबाय व्यवस्था तथा बाद में विस्तारित कोष सुविधा (Extended Fund Facility) हेतु अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष (IMF) से संपर्क किया और विश्व बैंक से भी ऋण लिया। ऋण अवमूल्यन, राजकोषीय घाटे में कमी तथा व्यापार उदारीकरण की शर्तों के साथ दिए गए, जिन्होंने LPG सुधारों को आकार दिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• IMF की स्थापना ब्रेटन वुड्स सम्मेलन (1944) में हुई और इसने 1945 से कार्य आरंभ किया; इसका मुख्यालय वाशिंगटन डी.सी. में है।<br>• IMF भुगतान संतुलन की समस्याओं के समाधान हेतु अल्पकालिक ऋण देता है, जबकि विश्व बैंक दीर्घकालिक विकास परियोजनाओं का वित्तपोषण करता है।<br>• विश्व व्यापार संगठन (WTO) की स्थापना 1995 में जिनेवा मुख्यालय के साथ, एशियाई विकास बैंक (ADB) की 1966 में मनीला में तथा यूरोपीय केंद्रीय बैंक (ECB) की 1998 में फ्रैंकफर्ट में हुई।<br>• संकट के समय धन जुटाने के लिए भारत ने 1991 में अपने स्वर्ण भंडार का एक भाग बैंक ऑफ इंग्लैंड में गिरवी रखा था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000073326","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Human Geography","question":{"en":"Mortality, fertility, and migration together primarily determine which of the following characteristics of a population? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मृत्यु-दर, प्रजनन-दर और प्रवास मिलकर मुख्य रूप से जनसंख्या की निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी विशेषता निर्धारित करते हैं? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Inflation trends and price levels","hi":"मुद्रास्फीति की प्रवृत्तियाँ और मूल्य स्तर"},"2":{"en":"Population size and composition","hi":"जनसंख्या का आकार और संरचना"},"3":{"en":"Gross domestic product growth","hi":"सकल घरेलू उत्पाद की वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"Fiscal stability and public expenditure","hi":"राजकोषीय स्थिरता और सार्वजनिक व्यय"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Population size and composition</b><br>Births (fertility), deaths (mortality) and migration are the three components of population change. Their balance decides how many people live in an area and how they are distributed by age and sex, that is, the size and composition of the population.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Natural increase of population = birth rate − death rate; when migration is added, it gives the actual growth of population.<br>• India’s population as per Census 2011 was <b>121.09 crore</b>, with a decadal growth of 17.7% and a sex ratio of <b>943</b> females per 1000 males.<br>• The <b>demographic transition theory</b> has four stages — high stationary, early expanding, late expanding and low stationary.<br>• India is in the third stage of demographic transition, with a falling birth rate, and is called a country of \"demographic dividend\" because of its young working-age population.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – जनसंख्या का आकार और संरचना</b><br>जन्म (प्रजनन-दर), मृत्यु (मृत्यु-दर) तथा प्रवास जनसंख्या परिवर्तन के तीन घटक हैं। इनका संतुलन यह निर्धारित करता है कि किसी क्षेत्र में कितने लोग रहते हैं और आयु व लिंग के आधार पर उनका वितरण कैसा है, अर्थात् जनसंख्या का आकार एवं संरचना।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जनसंख्या की प्राकृतिक वृद्धि = जन्म-दर − मृत्यु-दर; इसमें प्रवास जोड़ने पर जनसंख्या की वास्तविक वृद्धि प्राप्त होती है।<br>• जनगणना 2011 के अनुसार भारत की जनसंख्या 121.09 करोड़ थी, दशकीय वृद्धि 17.7% तथा लिंगानुपात प्रति 1000 पुरुषों पर 943 महिलाएँ था।<br>• जनसंख्या संक्रमण सिद्धांत (Demographic transition theory) के चार चरण हैं — उच्च स्थिर, प्रारंभिक विस्तार, उत्तर विस्तार तथा निम्न स्थिर।<br>• भारत संक्रमण के तीसरे चरण में है जहाँ जन्म-दर घट रही है, तथा युवा कार्यशील जनसंख्या के कारण इसे \"जनसांख्यिकीय लाभांश\" (Demographic dividend) वाला देश कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000073327","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which department is primarily responsible for promoting and coordinating Ease of Doing Business (EoDB) reforms in India? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में कारोबार सुगमता (EoDB) सुधारों को बढ़ावा देने तथा उनका समन्वयन करने का प्राथमिक दायित्व किस विभाग का है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade under the Ministry of Commerce and Industry","hi":"वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत उद्योग एवं आंतरिक व्यापार संवर्धन विभाग"},"2":{"en":"Department of Legal Affairs under the Ministry of Law and Justice","hi":"विधि एवं न्याय मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत विधि कार्य विभाग"},"3":{"en":"Department of Economic Affairs under the Ministry of Finance","hi":"वित्त मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत आर्थिक कार्य विभाग"},"4":{"en":"Development Monitoring and Evaluation Office under NITI Aayog","hi":"नीति आयोग के अंतर्गत विकास निगरानी एवं मूल्यांकन कार्यालय"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade under the Ministry of Commerce and Industry</b><br>The Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT) is the nodal department for coordinating Ease of Doing Business reforms in India. It works with states and ministries on regulatory simplification, single-window clearance and reduction of compliance burden.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• DPIIT, under the <b>Ministry of Commerce and Industry</b>, is also the nodal body for <b>Startup India, Make in India</b>, FDI policy, IPR and industrial policy.<br>• The World Bank’s Doing Business report was discontinued in <b>2021</b> and replaced by the <b>Business Ready (B-READY)</b> report from 2024.<br>• India’s rank in the last Doing Business report (2020) was <b>63rd</b>, a jump of 79 places from 142nd in 2014.<br>• DPIIT has launched the <b>National Single Window System</b> and the Jan Vishwas Act to decriminalise minor business offences.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत उद्योग एवं आंतरिक व्यापार संवर्धन विभाग</b><br>उद्योग एवं आंतरिक व्यापार संवर्धन विभाग (DPIIT) भारत में कारोबार सुगमता सुधारों के समन्वयन का नोडल विभाग है। यह राज्यों एवं मंत्रालयों के साथ मिलकर नियामकीय सरलीकरण, एकल-खिड़की अनुमोदन तथा अनुपालन बोझ में कमी पर कार्य करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्रालय के अंतर्गत DPIIT स्टार्टअप इंडिया, मेक इन इंडिया, FDI नीति, बौद्धिक संपदा अधिकार तथा औद्योगिक नीति का भी नोडल निकाय है।<br>• विश्व बैंक की डूइंग बिज़नेस रिपोर्ट 2021 में बंद कर दी गई और 2024 से बिज़नेस रेडी (B-READY) रिपोर्ट द्वारा प्रतिस्थापित की गई।<br>• अंतिम डूइंग बिज़नेस रिपोर्ट (2020) में भारत का स्थान 63वाँ था, जो 2014 के 142वें स्थान से 79 पायदान ऊपर था।<br>• DPIIT ने राष्ट्रीय एकल खिड़की प्रणाली (National Single Window System) तथा मामूली व्यापारिक अपराधों को अपराधमुक्त करने वाला जन विश्वास अधिनियम लागू किया है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000073328","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"Which of the following was a specific, monitorable social target set out in India’s Eleventh Five-Year Plan (2007–2012)? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा भारत की ग्यारहवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (2007–2012) में निर्धारित एक विशिष्ट, निगरानी योग्य सामाजिक लक्ष्य था? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reducing child malnutrition","hi":"बाल कुपोषण को कम करना"},"2":{"en":"Expanding defence production","hi":"रक्षा उत्पादन का विस्तार"},"3":{"en":"Increasing customs revenue","hi":"सीमा शुल्क राजस्व में वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"Privatising public enterprises","hi":"सार्वजनिक उद्यमों का निजीकरण"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Reducing child malnutrition</b><br>The Eleventh Five-Year Plan (2007–12) set 27 monitorable targets, including a specific social target to reduce malnutrition among children of the age group <b>0–3 years by half</b>. The plan had the theme of \"Faster and More Inclusive Growth\".<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Eleventh Plan targeted a GDP growth of <b>9%</b> and a farm sector growth of 4%.<br>• Other monitorable targets included reducing poverty by 10 percentage points, dropout rates in elementary schools, infant mortality rate to 28 per 1000 and maternal mortality ratio to 1 per 1000 live births.<br>• The Twelfth Plan (2012–17) was the last Five-Year Plan, with the theme \"Faster, More Inclusive and Sustainable Growth\".<br>• The Planning Commission was replaced by <b>NITI Aayog on 1 January 2015</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बाल कुपोषण को कम करना</b><br>ग्यारहवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (2007–12) में 27 निगरानी योग्य लक्ष्य निर्धारित किए गए थे, जिनमें 0–3 वर्ष आयु वर्ग के बच्चों में कुपोषण को आधा करने का विशिष्ट सामाजिक लक्ष्य भी सम्मिलित था। योजना का विषय \"तीव्रतर और अधिक समावेशी विकास\" था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ग्यारहवीं योजना में 9% GDP वृद्धि तथा कृषि क्षेत्र में 4% वृद्धि का लक्ष्य रखा गया।<br>• अन्य निगरानी योग्य लक्ष्यों में गरीबी को 10 प्रतिशत बिंदु तक घटाना, प्रारंभिक विद्यालयों में ड्रॉपआउट दर में कमी, शिशु मृत्यु दर 28 प्रति 1000 तथा मातृ मृत्यु अनुपात 1 प्रति 1000 जीवित जन्म करना सम्मिलित था।<br>• बारहवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (2012–17) अंतिम पंचवर्षीय योजना थी, जिसका विषय \"तीव्रतर, अधिक समावेशी और धारणीय विकास\" था।<br>• 1 जनवरी 2015 को योजना आयोग के स्थान पर नीति आयोग की स्थापना की गई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000073329","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Gandhian Era","question":{"en":"Which of the following leaders played a major organisational role in the Kheda Satyagraha? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किस नेता ने खेड़ा सत्याग्रह में प्रमुख संगठनात्मक भूमिका निभाई? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Motilal Nehru","hi":"मोतीलाल नेहरू"},"2":{"en":"Chittaranjan Das","hi":"चित्तरंजन दास"},"3":{"en":"Vallabhbhai Patel","hi":"वल्लभभाई पटेल"},"4":{"en":"Subhas Chandra Bose","hi":"सुभाष चंद्र बोस"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Vallabhbhai Patel</b><br>The Kheda Satyagraha of <b>1918</b> was organised in Kheda district of Gujarat against the collection of land revenue when the crops had failed. Gandhiji guided the movement, while <b>Vallabhbhai Patel</b> and his colleagues led its organisation at the ground level, which earned him the title \"Sardar\".<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Kheda Satyagraha was the first struggle in which <b>Gandhiji’s leadership</b> was accepted in a peasant movement in India; the government finally agreed to suspend revenue collection.<br>• It was followed by the <b>Ahmedabad Mill Strike (1918)</b>, where Gandhiji used the hunger strike for the first time.<br>• Vallabhbhai Patel was later given the title <b>\"Sardar\"</b> after leading the <b>Bardoli Satyagraha (1928)</b>.<br>• Gandhiji’s first satyagraha in India was the <b>Champaran Satyagraha (1917)</b> against indigo planters, while the Kheda struggle took place in the same period as the Rowlatt Satyagraha of 1919.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – वल्लभभाई पटेल</b><br>1918 का खेड़ा सत्याग्रह गुजरात के खेड़ा जिले में फसल खराब होने पर भू-राजस्व वसूली के विरुद्ध चलाया गया। गांधीजी ने आंदोलन का मार्गदर्शन किया, जबकि वल्लभभाई पटेल तथा उनके सहयोगियों ने भूमि स्तर पर इसका संगठन संभाला, जिसके कारण उन्हें \"सरदार\" की उपाधि मिली।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• खेड़ा सत्याग्रह वह पहला आंदोलन था जिसमें भारत में किसान आंदोलन के नेतृत्व के रूप में गांधीजी की स्वीकार्यता स्थापित हुई; अंततः सरकार राजस्व वसूली स्थगित करने पर सहमत हुई।<br>• इसके बाद अहमदाबाद मिल हड़ताल (1918) हुई, जहाँ गांधीजी ने पहली बार भूख हड़ताल का प्रयोग किया।<br>• बाद में बारदोली सत्याग्रह (1928) का नेतृत्व करने के बाद वल्लभभाई पटेल को \"सरदार\" की उपाधि दी गई।<br>• भारत में गांधीजी का पहला सत्याग्रह नील उत्पादकों के विरुद्ध चंपारण सत्याग्रह (1917) था, जबकि खेड़ा संघर्ष 1919 के रौलट सत्याग्रह के समान कालखंड का था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000073330","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"In a pond ecosystem, pesticide exposure causes a substantial decline in the population of fish that help regulate aquatic insect populations. After some time, the mosquito population increases rapidly. What is the most likely ecological explanation for this increase? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक तालाब पारितंत्र में कीटनाशक के संपर्क में आने से उन मछलियों की संख्या में काफी कमी आ जाती है जो जलीय कीटों की संख्या नियंत्रित करने में सहायक होती हैं। कुछ समय बाद मच्छरों की संख्या तेजी से बढ़ जाती है। इस वृद्धि की सर्वाधिक संभावित पारिस्थितिक व्याख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reduced competition among mosquito larvae for aquatic resources","hi":"जलीय संसाधनों के लिए मच्छर लार्वा के बीच प्रतिस्पर्धा में कमी"},"2":{"en":"Increased reproductive activity of mosquitoes due to pesticide exposure","hi":"कीटनाशक के संपर्क के कारण मच्छरों की प्रजनन क्रिया में वृद्धि"},"3":{"en":"Reduced predation on mosquito larvae following the decline in fish population","hi":"मछली संख्या में कमी के बाद मच्छर लार्वा पर परभक्षण में कमी"},"4":{"en":"Decreased water temperature leading to greater mosquito survival","hi":"जल के तापमान में कमी से मच्छरों की अधिक उत्तरजीविता"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Reduced predation on mosquito larvae following the decline in fish population</b><br>Fish such as Gambusia feed on mosquito larvae and keep their numbers in check. When pesticides kill these fish, predation pressure on the larvae falls, so larval survival and adult emergence rise sharply — a classic predator–prey (top-down) effect in the pond ecosystem.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A food chain shows one-way energy flow; the <b>10% law</b> given by Lindeman states that only about 10% energy passes to the next trophic level.<br>• Pesticides get concentrated at higher trophic levels through <b>biomagnification</b>, which harms fish, birds and humans.<br>• Biological control uses larvivorous fish like <b>Gambusia and guppy</b> to control mosquitoes, while Bti is a bacterial larvicide.<br>• An ecosystem has two components — <b>biotic</b> (producers, consumers, decomposers) and <b>abiotic</b> (light, temperature, water, soil); a pond is a natural aquatic ecosystem.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – मछली संख्या में कमी के बाद मच्छर लार्वा पर परभक्षण में कमी</b><br>गैंबुसिया जैसी मछलियाँ मच्छर लार्वा को खाकर उनकी संख्या नियंत्रित रखती हैं। जब कीटनाशक इन मछलियों को नष्ट कर देते हैं तो लार्वा पर परभक्षण का दबाव घट जाता है, जिससे लार्वा की उत्तरजीविता तथा वयस्क मच्छरों का उद्भव तेजी से बढ़ जाता है — यह तालाब पारितंत्र में परभक्षी–शिकार (ऊपर से नीचे) प्रभाव का उत्कृष्ट उदाहरण है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• खाद्य शृंखला में ऊर्जा का एकमार्गी प्रवाह होता है; लिंडमैन के 10% नियम के अनुसार केवल लगभग 10% ऊर्जा अगले पोषण स्तर तक पहुँचती है।<br>• कीटनाशक जैव आवर्धन (Biomagnification) द्वारा उच्च पोषण स्तरों पर सांद्रित होते हैं, जिससे मछली, पक्षी और मनुष्य प्रभावित होते हैं।<br>• जैविक नियंत्रण में मच्छरों को नियंत्रित करने हेतु गैंबुसिया व गप्पी जैसी लार्वाभक्षी मछलियों का उपयोग होता है, जबकि Bti एक जीवाणु लार्वानाशक है।<br>• पारितंत्र के दो घटक होते हैं — जैविक (उत्पादक, उपभोक्ता, अपघटक) तथा अजैविक (प्रकाश, तापमान, जल, मृत्तिका); तालाब एक प्राकृतिक जलीय पारितंत्र है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000073331","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The base of a right prism is a triangle with sides 5 cm, 12 cm, and 13 cm. The height of the prism is 9 cm. Find the lateral surface area. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज़्म का आधार 5 cm, 12 cm और 13 cm भुजाओं वाला त्रिभुज है। प्रिज़्म की ऊँचाई 9 cm है। पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"270 cm²"},"2":{"en":"380 cm²"},"3":{"en":"420 cm²"},"4":{"en":"440 cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"262\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"-17 0 262 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 196L218 196M26 52L218 52M26 196L26 52M218 52L66 26M218 196L218 52M66 26L26 52\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M218 196L66 170M66 170L26 196M66 170L66 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"2\" y=\"128\">9 cm</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"212\">12</text><text x=\"39\" y=\"176\">5</text></g></svg><br>Perimeter of base \\(= 5 + 12 + 13 = 30\\) cm<br>Lateral surface area \\(= 30 \\times 9\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{270\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 270 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"262\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"-17 0 262 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 196L218 196M26 52L218 52M26 196L26 52M218 52L66 26M218 196L218 52M66 26L26 52\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M218 196L66 170M66 170L26 196M66 170L66 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"2\" y=\"128\">9 cm</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"212\">12</text><text x=\"39\" y=\"176\">5</text></g></svg><br>आधार का परिमाप \\(= 5 + 12 + 13 = 30\\) cm<br>पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल \\(= 30 \\times 9\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{270\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 270 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000073332","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In an equilateral triangle, the centroid divides each median in a 2:1 ratio. What is the distance between the centroid and the nine-point center in an equilateral triangle? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समबाहु त्रिभुज में केंद्रक प्रत्येक माध्यिका को 2:1 अनुपात में विभाजित करता है। एक समबाहु त्रिभुज में केंद्रक और नवबिंदु केंद्र के बीच की दूरी क्या है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Zero","hi":"शून्य"},"2":{"en":"One-third of the circumradius","hi":"परित्रिज्या की एक-तिहाई"},"3":{"en":"Equal to the circumradius","hi":"परित्रिज्या के बराबर"},"4":{"en":"Half the circumradius","hi":"परित्रिज्या की आधी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In an equilateral triangle the centroid, orthocentre, circumcentre and nine-point centre all coincide<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{Zero}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Zero.</b>","hi":"समबाहु त्रिभुज में केंद्रक, लंबकेंद्र, परिकेंद्र और नवबिंदु केंद्र सभी एक ही बिंदु पर होते हैं<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{शून्य}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): शून्य है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000073333","section":"MATH","topic":"LCM and HCF","question":{"en":"Find the smallest square number that is divisible by each of the numbers 4, 9, and 10. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"4, 9 और 10 में से प्रत्येक से विभाज्य न्यूनतम वर्ग संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"500"},"2":{"en":"900"},"3":{"en":"600"},"4":{"en":"700"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\text{LCM}(4,9,10) = 180 = 2^2 \\times 3^2 \\times 5\\)<br>Multiply by 5 to complete the square<br>\\(180 \\times 5 = \\boxed{900}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 900.</b>","hi":"\\(\\text{LCM}(4,9,10) = 180 = 2^2 \\times 3^2 \\times 5\\)<br>वर्ग पूरा करने के लिए 5 से गुणा कीजिए<br>\\(180 \\times 5 = \\boxed{900}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 900 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000073334","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"A and B invest in a business such that A's capital is used for 7 months and B's for 9 months. If the profit is shared in the ratio 7 : 10 and A's investment is ₹1,800 less than B's, find the total capital invested by both. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A और B एक व्यवसाय में निवेश करते हैं जिसमें A की पूँजी 7 माह और B की 9 माह के लिए लगी रहती है। यदि लाभ 7 : 10 के अनुपात में बाँटा जाता है और A का निवेश B से ₹1,800 कम है, तो दोनों का कुल निवेश ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹38,230"},"2":{"en":"₹34,200"},"3":{"en":"₹27,220"},"4":{"en":"₹44,100"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{7A}{9B} = \\frac{7}{10} \\Rightarrow \\frac{A}{B} = \\frac{9}{10}\\)<br>Let A \\(= 9x\\), B \\(= 10x\\); \\(x = 1800\\)<br>Total \\(= 19 \\times 1800 = \\boxed{34{,}200}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹34,200.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{7A}{9B} = \\frac{7}{10} \\Rightarrow \\frac{A}{B} = \\frac{9}{10}\\)<br>A \\(= 9x\\), B \\(= 10x\\); \\(x = 1800\\)<br>कुल \\(= 19 \\times 1800 = \\boxed{34{,}200}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹34,200 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000073335","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"Find the amount after 3 years if ₹12,000 is invested at 15% per annum compound interest. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि ₹12,000 15% प्रतिवर्ष चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर निवेश किए जाएँ, तो 3 वर्ष बाद मिश्रधन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹18250.50"},"2":{"en":"₹17250.50"},"3":{"en":"₹19250.50"},"4":{"en":"₹16250.50"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(A = 12000(1.15)^3\\)<br>\\(= 12000 \\times 1.520875\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{18250.50}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹18250.50.</b>","hi":"\\(A = 12000(1.15)^3\\)<br>\\(= 12000 \\times 1.520875\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{18250.50}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹18250.50 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000073336","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"The ratio of the number of sides of two regular polygons is 1:2 and the ratio of their interior angles is 3:4. Find the number of sides of these polygons. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो सम बहुभुजों की भुजाओं की संख्या का अनुपात 1:2 और उनके अंतःकोणों का अनुपात 3:4 है। इन बहुभुजों की भुजाओं की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 sides and 30 sides","hi":"15 भुजाएँ और 30 भुजाएँ"},"2":{"en":"3 sides and 6 sides","hi":"3 भुजाएँ और 6 भुजाएँ"},"3":{"en":"5 sides and 10 sides","hi":"5 भुजाएँ और 10 भुजाएँ"},"4":{"en":"7 sides and 14 sides","hi":"7 भुजाएँ और 14 भुजाएँ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Sides \\(n\\) and \\(2n\\); interior angles \\(\\frac{180(n-2)}{n}\\) and \\(\\frac{180(2n-2)}{2n}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{n-2}{n} : \\frac{2n-2}{2n} = 3 : 4 \\Rightarrow \\frac{n-2}{n-1} = \\frac{3}{4}\\)<br>\\(n = 5\\) and \\(10\\): \\(\\boxed{5\\ \\text{sides and}\\ 10\\ \\text{sides}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 5 sides and 10 sides.</b>","hi":"भुजाएँ \\(n\\) और \\(2n\\); अंतःकोण \\(\\frac{180(n-2)}{n}\\) और \\(\\frac{180(2n-2)}{2n}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{n-2}{n} : \\frac{2n-2}{2n} = 3 : 4 \\Rightarrow \\frac{n-2}{n-1} = \\frac{3}{4}\\)<br>\\(n = 5\\) और \\(10\\): \\(\\boxed{5\\ \\text{भुजाएँ और}\\ 10\\ \\text{भुजाएँ}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 5 भुजाएँ और 10 भुजाएँ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000073337","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"If the perimeter of a semicircle is 47.1 cm, what is its approximate diameter? (Take π = 3.14) [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि एक अर्धवृत्त का परिमाप 47.1 cm है, तो उसका अनुमानित व्यास क्या है? (π = 3.14 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15.4 cm"},"2":{"en":"17.5 cm"},"3":{"en":"16.8 cm"},"4":{"en":"18.3 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"242\" height=\"147\" viewBox=\"0 0 242 147\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 121L216 121M216 121A95 95 0 0 0 26 121\"/><circle cx=\"121\" cy=\"121\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"168\" y=\"137\">r</text><text x=\"74\" y=\"137\">r</text><text x=\"121\" y=\"22\">πr</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\pi r + 2r = 47.1\\)<br>\\(r(5.14) = 47.1 \\Rightarrow r = 9.16\\)<br>Diameter \\(\\approx \\boxed{18.3\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 18.3 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"242\" height=\"147\" viewBox=\"0 0 242 147\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 121L216 121M216 121A95 95 0 0 0 26 121\"/><circle cx=\"121\" cy=\"121\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"168\" y=\"137\">r</text><text x=\"74\" y=\"137\">r</text><text x=\"121\" y=\"22\">πr</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\pi r + 2r = 47.1\\)<br>\\(r(5.14) = 47.1 \\Rightarrow r = 9.16\\)<br>व्यास \\(\\approx \\boxed{18.3\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 18.3 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000073338","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A conical tent of radius 7 m and height 24 m is to be covered using cloth of width 4 m. Find the approximate length of cloth required. Take (π = 22/7) [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"7 m त्रिज्या और 24 m ऊँचाई वाले शंक्वाकार तंबू को 4 m चौड़े कपड़े से ढकना है। आवश्यक कपड़े की अनुमानित लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। (π = 22/7 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"138 m"},"2":{"en":"118 m"},"3":{"en":"128 m"},"4":{"en":"148 m"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"143\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 143 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 181A45 15 0 0 0 117 181M26 181L71 26L117 181M77 181L77 175L71 175\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 181A45 15 0 0 1 117 181M71 26L71 181M71 181L117 181\"/><circle cx=\"71\" cy=\"181\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"101\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">24 m</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"195\" font-size=\"11\">7 m</text><text x=\"37\" y=\"104\">l</text></g></svg><br>\\(l = \\sqrt{7^2 + 24^2} = 25\\) m<br>CSA \\(= \\pi r l = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7 \\times 25 = 550\\ \\text{m}^2\\)<br>Length \\(= \\frac{550}{4} = 137.5 \\approx \\boxed{138\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 138 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"143\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 143 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 181A45 15 0 0 0 117 181M26 181L71 26L117 181M77 181L77 175L71 175\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 181A45 15 0 0 1 117 181M71 26L71 181M71 181L117 181\"/><circle cx=\"71\" cy=\"181\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"101\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">24 m</text><text x=\"94\" y=\"195\" font-size=\"11\">7 m</text><text x=\"37\" y=\"104\">l</text></g></svg><br>\\(l = \\sqrt{7^2 + 24^2} = 25\\) m<br>CSA \\(= \\pi r l = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7 \\times 25 = 550\\ \\text{m}^2\\)<br>लंबाई \\(= \\frac{550}{4} = 137.5 \\approx \\boxed{138\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 138 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000073339","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A man sells an article at a loss of 10%. Had he bought it for 20% less and sold it for ₹55 more, he could have gained 40%. What is the cost price? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति किसी वस्तु को 10% हानि पर बेचता है। यदि उसने उसे 20% कम पर खरीदा होता और ₹55 अधिक में बेचा होता, तो उसे 40% लाभ होता। क्रय मूल्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹250"},"2":{"en":"₹280"},"3":{"en":"₹200"},"4":{"en":"₹260"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Let CP \\(= C\\); SP \\(= 0.9C\\)<br>\\(0.9C + 55 = 1.40 \\times 0.8C = 1.12C\\)<br>\\(0.22C = 55 \\Rightarrow C = \\boxed{250}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹250.</b>","hi":"क्रय मूल्य \\(= C\\); विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 0.9C\\)<br>\\(0.9C + 55 = 1.40 \\times 0.8C = 1.12C\\)<br>\\(0.22C = 55 \\Rightarrow C = \\boxed{250}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹250 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000073340","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"The producer makes a profit of 15% by selling the product to the wholesaler. The wholesaler sells it to the retailer making 10% profit. The retailer sells it to the consumer for ₹12,903 making a profit of 2%. Find the cost of production of the product. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निर्माता उत्पाद को थोक व्यापारी को बेचकर 15% लाभ कमाता है। थोक व्यापारी उसे खुदरा व्यापारी को 10% लाभ पर बेचता है। खुदरा व्यापारी उसे उपभोक्ता को ₹12,903 में 2% लाभ पर बेचता है। उत्पाद की उत्पादन लागत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹20,000"},"2":{"en":"₹40,000"},"3":{"en":"₹10,000"},"4":{"en":"₹60,000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(C \\times 1.15 \\times 1.10 \\times 1.02 = 12903\\)<br>\\(C \\times 1.2903 = 12903\\)<br>\\(C = \\boxed{10{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹10,000.</b>","hi":"\\(C \\times 1.15 \\times 1.10 \\times 1.02 = 12903\\)<br>\\(C \\times 1.2903 = 12903\\)<br>\\(C = \\boxed{10{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹10,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000073341","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a triangle, the sides are 100, 150 and z units. How many integer values are possible for z? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक त्रिभुज की भुजाएँ 100, 150 और z इकाई हैं। z के कितने पूर्णांक मान संभव हैं? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"161"},"2":{"en":"199"},"3":{"en":"179"},"4":{"en":"130"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Triangle inequality: \\(150 - 100 < z < 150 + 100\\)<br>\\(50 < z < 250\\)<br>Integers \\(= 249 - 51 + 1 = \\boxed{199}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 199.</b>","hi":"त्रिभुज असमिका: \\(150 - 100 < z < 150 + 100\\)<br>\\(50 < z < 250\\)<br>पूर्णांक \\(= 249 - 51 + 1 = \\boxed{199}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 199 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000073342","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"Points A and B are on the same side of a tower. The angles of elevation of the top of the tower from A and B are 45° and 60° respectively. The approximate distance between A and B is 40 m. Find the height of the tower (Use √3 = 1.732) [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बिंदु A और B एक मीनार के एक ही ओर हैं। A और B से मीनार के शिखर के उन्नयन कोण क्रमशः 45° और 60° हैं। A और B के बीच की दूरी लगभग 40 m है। मीनार की ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए (√3 = 1.732 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"99 m"},"2":{"en":"95 m"},"3":{"en":"85 m"},"4":{"en":"90 m"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"202\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 202 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 176L176 176M26 176L26 26M34 176L34 168L26 168M113 176L26 26M95 176A18 18 0 0 1 104 160M176 176L26 26M158 176A18 18 0 0 1 163 163\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">P</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"187\">Q</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"105\">h</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"190\">B′</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"11\">45°</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"190\">A′</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"192\">x</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"192\">40 m</text></g></svg><br>\\(h\\cot 60° = \\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\), \\(h\\cot 45° = h\\)<br>\\(h - \\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}} = 40 \\Rightarrow h\\left(\\frac{0.732}{1.732}\\right) = 40\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{95\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 95 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"202\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 202 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 176L176 176M26 176L26 26M34 176L34 168L26 168M113 176L26 26M95 176A18 18 0 0 1 104 160M176 176L26 26M158 176A18 18 0 0 1 163 163\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\">P</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"187\">Q</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"105\">h</text><text x=\"87\" y=\"165\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"190\">B′</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"11\">45°</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"190\">A′</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"192\">x</text><text x=\"144\" y=\"192\">40 m</text></g></svg><br>\\(h\\cot 60° = \\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\), \\(h\\cot 45° = h\\)<br>\\(h - \\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}} = 40 \\Rightarrow h\\left(\\frac{0.732}{1.732}\\right) = 40\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{95\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 95 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000073343","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"What is the value of \\(\\frac{8\\cos^2 30° + 4\\sin^2 45° - 3\\operatorname{cosec}^2 60°}{2\\tan^2 60° - 6\\operatorname{cosec} 30°}\\)? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\\(\\frac{8\\cos^2 30° + 4\\sin^2 45° - 3\\operatorname{cosec}^2 60°}{2\\tan^2 60° - 6\\operatorname{cosec} 30°}\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{-2}{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Numerator \\(= 8\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) + 4\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) - 3\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right) = 6 + 2 - 4 = 4\\)<br>Denominator \\(= 2(3) - 6(2) = 6 - 12 = -6\\)<br>\\(\\frac{4}{-6} = \\boxed{\\frac{-2}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{-2}{3}\\).</b>","hi":"अंश \\(= 8\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) + 4\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) - 3\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right) = 6 + 2 - 4 = 4\\)<br>हर \\(= 2(3) - 6(2) = 6 - 12 = -6\\)<br>\\(\\frac{4}{-6} = \\boxed{\\frac{-2}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{-2}{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000073344","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A solid sphere of radius 10 cm is melted and recast into small cones, each with a radius of 2.5 cm and a height of 8 cm. How many cones can be formed? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"10 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक ठोस गोले को पिघलाकर 2.5 cm त्रिज्या और 8 cm ऊँचाई वाले छोटे शंकु बनाए जाते हैं। कितने शंकु बन सकते हैं? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20"},"2":{"en":"40"},"3":{"en":"60"},"4":{"en":"80"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Sphere volume \\(= \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (1000) = \\frac{4000\\pi}{3}\\)<br>Cone volume \\(= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi (6.25)(8) = \\frac{50\\pi}{3}\\)<br>Number \\(= \\frac{4000}{50} = \\boxed{80}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 80.</b>","hi":"गोले का आयतन \\(= \\frac{4}{3}\\pi (1000) = \\frac{4000\\pi}{3}\\)<br>शंकु का आयतन \\(= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi (6.25)(8) = \\frac{50\\pi}{3}\\)<br>संख्या \\(= \\frac{4000}{50} = \\boxed{80}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 80 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000073345","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, D and E lie on AB and AC such that DE is parallel to BC. If AD: DB = 5: 3 and AE = 15 cm, find AC. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, D और E भुजाओं AB और AC पर इस प्रकार हैं कि DE, BC के समांतर है। यदि AD: DB = 5: 3 और AE = 15 cm है, तो AC ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 cm"},"2":{"en":"18 cm"},"3":{"en":"24 cm"},"4":{"en":"27 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"256\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M94 26L26 196L230 196ZM52 132L179 132\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"244\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"41\" y=\"136\">D</text><text x=\"189\" y=\"136\">E</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"78\">5</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"163\">3</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"74\">15</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{AE}{AC}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{5}{8} = \\frac{15}{AC}\\)<br>\\(AC = \\boxed{24\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 24 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"256\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M94 26L26 196L230 196ZM52 132L179 132\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"16\">A</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"207\">B</text><text x=\"244\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"41\" y=\"136\">D</text><text x=\"189\" y=\"136\">E</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"78\">5</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"163\">3</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"74\">15</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{AE}{AC}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{5}{8} = \\frac{15}{AC}\\)<br>\\(AC = \\boxed{24\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 24 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000073346","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"What is the value of 999² − 998²? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"999² − 998² का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1995"},"2":{"en":"1997"},"3":{"en":"1999"},"4":{"en":"2001"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)\\)<br>\\(= (1997)(1)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1997}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1997.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)\\)<br>\\(= (1997)(1)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1997}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1997 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000073347","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A company borrowed ₹10,00,000. One-fourth of the loan was repaid after 4 years and another one-third of the original loan after 7 years. The remaining principal was cleared after 10 years. If the simple interest rate was 9% per annum, calculate the total interest paid. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक कंपनी ने ₹10,00,000 उधार लिए। 4 वर्ष बाद ऋण का एक-चौथाई और 7 वर्ष बाद मूल ऋण का एक-तिहाई चुकाया गया। शेष मूलधन 10 वर्ष बाद चुकाया गया। यदि साधारण ब्याज दर 9% प्रति वर्ष थी, तो कुल दिया गया ब्याज ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹6,75,000"},"2":{"en":"₹6,60,000"},"3":{"en":"₹6,20,000"},"4":{"en":"₹6,00,000"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{10^6 \\times 9 \\times 4}{100} + \\frac{7.5 \\times 10^5 \\times 9 \\times 3}{100} + \\frac{4.167 \\times 10^5 \\times 9 \\times 3}{100}\\)<br>\\(= 360000 + 202500 + 112500\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6{,}75{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹6,75,000.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{10^6 \\times 9 \\times 4}{100} + \\frac{7.5 \\times 10^5 \\times 9 \\times 3}{100} + \\frac{4.167 \\times 10^5 \\times 9 \\times 3}{100}\\)<br>\\(= 360000 + 202500 + 112500\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6{,}75{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹6,75,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000073348","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If tanA = m and A is an acute angle, what is the value of cosA? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि tanA = m और A न्यून कोण है, तो cosA का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{m}{\\sqrt{1+m^2}}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+m^2}}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{1+m^2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1-m}{\\sqrt{1+m^2}}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sec^2 A = 1 + \\tan^2 A = 1 + m^2\\)<br>\\(\\cos A = \\frac{1}{\\sec A}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+m^2}}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+m^2}}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\sec^2 A = 1 + \\tan^2 A = 1 + m^2\\)<br>\\(\\cos A = \\frac{1}{\\sec A}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+m^2}}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+m^2}}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000073349","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"A tank is connected to 15 pipes. Some of these are inlet pipes, while the remaining are outlet pipes. An inlet pipe alone can fill the tank in 8 hrs. On the other hand, an outlet pipe alone can empty the tank in 6 hrs. The tank is emptied in 6 hrs if all the pipes are opened simultaneously when the tank is exactly full. Find out how many of the pipes are outlet pipes. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक टंकी 15 पाइपों से जुड़ी है। इनमें से कुछ भरने वाले पाइप और शेष निकालने वाले पाइप हैं। एक भरने वाला पाइप अकेला टंकी को 8 घंटे में भर सकता है। दूसरी ओर एक निकालने वाला पाइप अकेला टंकी को 6 घंटे में खाली कर सकता है। यदि टंकी पूरी भरी होने पर सभी पाइप एक साथ खोले जाएँ, तो टंकी 6 घंटे में खाली हो जाती है। ज्ञात कीजिए कि कितने पाइप निकालने वाले हैं। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"7"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let outlets be \\(x\\), inlets \\(15 - x\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x}{6} - \\frac{15 - x}{8} = \\frac{1}{6}\\)<br>\\(4x - 3(15 - x) = 4 \\Rightarrow 7x = 49 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{7}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 7.</b>","hi":"निकासी पाइप \\(x\\), भरण पाइप \\(15 - x\\) मानिए<br>\\(\\frac{x}{6} - \\frac{15 - x}{8} = \\frac{1}{6}\\)<br>\\(4x - 3(15 - x) = 4 \\Rightarrow 7x = 49 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{7}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 7 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000073350","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"A cistern is initially empty. Inlet pipes A and B fill it at constant rates of \\(\\frac{1}{12}\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) of the cistern per hour, respectively, while outlet pipe C empties it at a constant rate of \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) per hour. Sumeet opens pipes A and B at time zero. Under his original plan, pipe C is programmed to start instantly when the cistern reaches 50%, and Sumeet returns exactly at the moment the cistern becomes completely full.<br>However, due to a malfunction, pipe C starts instantly when the cistern is \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) full instead. All active pipes run continuously and simultaneously, and the cistern level always stays between 0% and 100%.<br>When Sumeet returns at the originally planned time and stops all pipes, what percentage of the cistern is filled? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक टंकी प्रारंभ में खाली है। भरने वाले पाइप A और B इसे क्रमशः \\(\\frac{1}{12}\\) और \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) प्रति घंटा की दर से भरते हैं, जबकि निकालने वाला पाइप C इसे \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) प्रति घंटा की दर से खाली करता है। सुमीत समय शून्य पर पाइप A और B खोलता है। उसकी मूल योजना में पाइप C तब तुरंत चालू होता है जब टंकी 50% तक भर जाती है, और सुमीत ठीक उस क्षण लौटता है जब टंकी पूरी भर जाती है।<br>परंतु खराबी के कारण पाइप C तब चालू होता है जब टंकी \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) भरी होती है। सभी सक्रिय पाइप लगातार और एक साथ चलते हैं, तथा टंकी का स्तर सदैव 0% से 100% के बीच रहता है।<br>जब सुमीत मूल योजना के समय पर लौटकर सभी पाइप बंद करता है, तो टंकी का कितना प्रतिशत भरा होता है? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"75%"},"2":{"en":"80%"},"3":{"en":"85%"},"4":{"en":"90%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A + B \\(= \\frac{1}{12} + \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{5}{24}\\) per hour<br>Original plan: 50% in \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\div \\frac{5}{24} = 2.4\\) h; with C on, net \\(= \\frac{5}{24} - \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{1}{12}\\) per hour, so another 6 h; total 8.4 h<br>New: \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) filled in 1.6 h, then net \\(\\frac{1}{12}\\) per hour for 6.8 h\\(\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{6.8}{12}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{3} + 0.5667 = 0.9 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{90\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 90%.</b>","hi":"A + B \\(= \\frac{1}{12} + \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{5}{24}\\) प्रति घंटा<br>मूल योजना: 50% भरने में \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\div \\frac{5}{24} = 2.4\\) घंटे; C चालू होने पर शुद्ध दर \\(= \\frac{5}{24} - \\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{1}{12}\\) प्रति घंटा, अतः 6 घंटे और; कुल 8.4 घंटे<br>नई स्थिति: 1.6 घंटे में \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) भरता है, फिर 6.8 घंटे \\(\\frac{1}{12}\\) प्रति घंटा \\(\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{6.8}{12}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{3} + 0.5667 = 0.9 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{90\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 90% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000073351","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate: sin² 25° + sin² 65° [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: sin² 25° + sin² 65° [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"1"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin 65° = \\cos 25°\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2 25° + \\cos^2 25°\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin 65° = \\cos 25°\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2 25° + \\cos^2 25°\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000073352","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If y + \\(\\frac{1}{y} = 17\\), find the value of \\(y^3 + \\frac{1}{y^3}\\). [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि y + \\(\\frac{1}{y} = 17\\) है, तो \\(y^3 + \\frac{1}{y^3}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4913"},"2":{"en":"4862"},"3":{"en":"4964"},"4":{"en":"4896"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(y^3 + \\frac{1}{y^3} = 17^3 - 3(17)\\)<br>\\(= 4913 - 51\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4862}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4862.</b>","hi":"\\(y^3 + \\frac{1}{y^3} = 17^3 - 3(17)\\)<br>\\(= 4913 - 51\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{4862}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4862 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000073353","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If a + b = 22 and ab = 85, evaluate a² + b². [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि a + b = 22 और ab = 85 है, तो a² + b² का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"308"},"2":{"en":"314"},"3":{"en":"326"},"4":{"en":"382"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab\\)<br>\\(= 484 - 170\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{314}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 314.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab\\)<br>\\(= 484 - 170\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{314}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 314 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000073354","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A solid regular hexagonal prism has a base side length of 5 m and a height of 12 m. All of its outer surfaces (including the top and bottom bases) are painted at a rate of Rs. 20 per m². Find the total painting cost (approximately). [Take √3 ≈ 1.732] [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक ठोस सम षट्कोणीय प्रिज़्म की आधार भुजा 5 m और ऊँचाई 12 m है। इसकी सभी बाहरी सतहें (ऊपरी और निचले आधार सहित) Rs. 20 प्रति m² की दर से रंगी जाती हैं। कुल पेंटिंग लागत (लगभग) ज्ञात कीजिए। [√3 ≈ 1.732 लीजिए] [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rs. 9798"},"2":{"en":"Rs. 8342"},"3":{"en":"Rs. 9000"},"4":{"en":"Rs. 8073"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"184\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"-15 0 184 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M143 41L137 26M143 181L143 41M137 26L78 26M78 26L26 41M26 181L32 196M26 41L32 55M26 181L26 41M32 196L91 196M32 55L91 55M32 196L32 55M91 196L143 181M91 55L143 41M91 196L91 55\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M143 181L137 167M137 167L78 167M137 167L137 26M78 167L26 181M78 167L78 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"3\" y=\"115\">12 m</text><text x=\"121\" y=\"207\">5 m</text></g></svg><br>Lateral surface \\(= 6 \\times 5 \\times 12 = 360\\ \\text{m}^2\\)<br>Two bases \\(= 2 \\times \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}(25) = 129.9\\ \\text{m}^2\\)<br>Total \\(= 489.9\\ \\text{m}^2\\); cost \\(= 489.9 \\times 20 \\approx \\boxed{9798}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Rs. 9798.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"184\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"-15 0 184 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M143 41L137 26M143 181L143 41M137 26L78 26M78 26L26 41M26 181L32 196M26 41L32 55M26 181L26 41M32 196L91 196M32 55L91 55M32 196L32 55M91 196L143 181M91 55L143 41M91 196L91 55\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M143 181L137 167M137 167L78 167M137 167L137 26M78 167L26 181M78 167L78 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"3\" y=\"115\">12 m</text><text x=\"121\" y=\"207\">5 m</text></g></svg><br>पार्श्व पृष्ठ \\(= 6 \\times 5 \\times 12 = 360\\ \\text{m}^2\\)<br>दोनों आधार \\(= 2 \\times \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}(25) = 129.9\\ \\text{m}^2\\)<br>कुल \\(= 489.9\\ \\text{m}^2\\); लागत \\(= 489.9 \\times 20 \\approx \\boxed{9798}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): Rs. 9798 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000073355","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{(a + \\sqrt{b})} = \\sqrt{x} + \\sqrt{y}\\), where a = 5, b = 21, and x, y are rational numbers, determine the value of x + y. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{(a + \\sqrt{b})} = \\sqrt{x} + \\sqrt{y}\\) है, जहाँ a = 5, b = 21, और x, y परिमेय संख्याएँ हैं, तो x + y का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"21"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(x + y = a = 5\\) and \\(4xy = b = 21\\)<br>Squaring both sides, the rational parts match: \\(x + y = 5\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 5.</b>","hi":"\\(x + y = a = 5\\) और \\(4xy = b = 21\\)<br>दोनों पक्षों का वर्ग करने पर परिमेय भाग मेल खाते हैं: \\(x + y = 5\\)<br>\\(\\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000073356","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>Despite the abstract nature of quantum mechanics,<br>P. mathematical formulations such as Hilbert spaces and wave functions<br>Q. to make remarkably accurate predictions<br>R. provide a rigorous framework<br>S. about the behaviour of subatomic particles [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PRQS"},"2":{"en":"PSQR"},"3":{"en":"RPQS"},"4":{"en":"QPRS"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: PRQS</b><br>P supplies the subject: mathematical formulations such as Hilbert spaces and wave functions.<br>R gives the predicate “provide a rigorous framework.”<br>Q states the purpose, and S specifies what the predictions concern.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): PRQS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000073357","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct transformation of the sentence into direct speech.<br>I told the children not to stay out too late. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"I said, “Don't stay out too late, children.”"},"2":{"en":"I said, “Don't stay out late, children.”"},"3":{"en":"I told, “You can't stay out too late, children.”"},"4":{"en":"I said, “Stay out too late, children.”"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Told + object + not to” becomes a negative imperative in direct speech.</b><br>“Not to stay out too late” becomes “Don’t stay out too late.”<br>B omits “too”; C incorrectly uses “told” without an object and changes the instruction.<br>D removes the negative and reverses the meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): I said, “Don't stay out too late, children.”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000073358","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “a snake in the grass” mean? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A loyal and trustworthy friend"},"2":{"en":"A secret or deceitful enemy"},"3":{"en":"A person who loves nature"},"4":{"en":"A shy and introverted person"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>A snake in the grass (छिपा हुआ शत्रु) = a treacherous person who pretends to be harmless.</b><br>Example: “He seemed friendly, but he proved to be a snake in the grass.”<br>A loyal friend is the opposite; loving nature and shyness do not imply deceit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A secret or deceitful enemy.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000073359","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br>He was complete ignored by the team during the discussion. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"during"},"2":{"en":"ignored"},"3":{"en":"complete"},"4":{"en":"team"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Use an adverb to modify the passive verb “was ignored.”</b><br>“Complete” is an adjective and must become “completely.”<br>Correct sentence: “He was <b>completely</b> ignored by the team during the discussion.”<br>The other parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): complete.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000073360","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the option that best improves the sentence by using the correct collocation highlighted in bold.<br>The company <b>reached a heavy loss</b> last quarter due to poor management. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"suffered a heavy loss"},"2":{"en":"reached a large loss"},"3":{"en":"made a hard loss"},"4":{"en":"got a strong loss"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Collocation: “Suffer a heavy loss” means experience a major financial loss.</b><br>Correct sentence: “The company <b>suffered a heavy loss</b> last quarter due to poor management.”<br>“Reached a large loss” is unidiomatic.<br>“Hard loss” and “strong loss” are not standard business collocations.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): suffered a heavy loss.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000073361","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Complete the sentence by choosing a suitable word to fill in the blank.<br>Had he not intervened, the negatiations ___ long before the deadline. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"would break"},"2":{"en":"had broken"},"3":{"en":"would have broken down"},"4":{"en":"should be breaking"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An inverted unreal past condition takes “would have + past participle” in the result.</b><br>“Break down” means collapse or fail, which fits negotiations.<br>Completed sentence: “Had he not intervened, the negatiations <b>would have broken down</b> long before the deadline.”<br>The other options do not form the required third-conditional result.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): would have broken down.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000073362","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. It was formed due to tectonic activity, where the Earth's crust is slowly pulling apart, creating deep fissures and valleys.<br>2. The Great Rift Valley in East Africa is one of the most significant geological formations on Earth.<br>3. The valley is home to some of the richest fossil sites, including discoveries of Australopithecus fossils that provide insights into early human ancestors.<br>4. Over time, the valley has influenced the course of human evolution, as early hominins adapted to its diverse environments.<br>5. Today, the region continues to be studied by geologists and anthropologists to understand both Earth's history and the origins of humankind. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-1-4-3-5"},"2":{"en":"3-1-4-5-2"},"3":{"en":"3-2-1-4-5"},"4":{"en":"5-4-3-2-1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-1-4-3-5</b><br>Sentence 2 introduces the Great Rift Valley, and sentence 1 explains its formation.<br>Sentence 4 describes its influence on human evolution; sentence 3 supports this with fossil discoveries.<br>Sentence 5 closes with continuing geological and anthropological research.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2-1-4-3-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000073363","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitution for the sentence below.<br>“Ravi is known for his ability to manage money wisely and never spends more than necessary.” [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Extravagant"},"2":{"en":"Prodigal"},"3":{"en":"Thrifty"},"4":{"en":"Spendthrift"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Thrifty (मितव्ययी) = careful with money and avoiding waste.</b><br><b>Extravagant (फिजूलखर्च)</b> = spending excessively<br><b>Prodigal (अपव्ययी)</b> = wastefully extravagant<br><b>Spendthrift (फिजूलखर्च)</b> = a person who spends money carelessly<br>Ravi’s careful money management makes him thrifty.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Thrifty.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000073364","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Which of the following refers to a group of stars that form a recognizable pattern in the sky? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Eclipse"},"2":{"en":"Constellation"},"3":{"en":"Meteor"},"4":{"en":"Asteroid"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Constellation (तारामंडल) = a recognizable pattern formed by a group of stars.</b><br><b>Eclipse (ग्रहण)</b> = obscuring of one celestial body by another<br><b>Meteor (उल्का)</b> = a streak of light from a meteoroid entering the atmosphere<br><b>Asteroid (क्षुद्रग्रह)</b> = a small rocky body orbiting the Sun<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Constellation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000073365","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Voluble</b> [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Talkative"},"2":{"en":"Garrulous"},"3":{"en":"Reticent"},"4":{"en":"Chatty"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Voluble (वाचाल) = speaking fluently and at length.</b><br><b>Talkative (बातूनी)</b> = fond of talking<br><b>Garrulous (अधिक बोलने वाला)</b> = excessively talkative<br><b>Reticent (अल्पभाषी)</b> = reserved and reluctant to speak ✔<br><b>Chatty (गपशप करने वाला)</b> = inclined to chat<br>More antonyms: taciturn, reserved, uncommunicative.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Reticent.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000073366","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br>Grain of salt [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Complete faith in something"},"2":{"en":"A hint of manipulation"},"3":{"en":"A cautious or skeptical attitude toward truth"},"4":{"en":"An excess of honesty"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Take something with a grain of salt (पूरी तरह विश्वास न करना)</b><br>It means regard a claim cautiously or sceptically rather than accept it completely.<br>Example: “Take his exaggerated story with a grain of salt.”<br>Complete faith is the opposite; manipulation and excessive honesty are unrelated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): A cautious or skeptical attitude toward truth.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000073367","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of word meaning “disguise or concealment” [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Camoflage"},"2":{"en":"Camouflage"},"3":{"en":"Camoflauge"},"4":{"en":"Camuoflage"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Camouflage (छलावरण) = disguise or concealment.</b><br>The correct spelling is “camouflage,” with “u” after “o.”<br><b>Camoflage</b> omits that “u”; <b>Camoflauge</b> omits “u” and reverses “au.”<br><b>Camuoflage</b> places “u” in the wrong position.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Camouflage.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000073368","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Select the correct option:<br>The operative complied, albeit ___ reluctance. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"with great"},"2":{"en":"in great"},"3":{"en":"on great"},"4":{"en":"at great"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “With reluctance” is the standard prepositional phrase.</b><br>“Great” intensifies the reluctance, and “albeit” introduces the concession.<br>Correct sentence: “The operative complied, albeit <b>with great</b> reluctance.”<br>“In,” “on” and “at” do not form the idiomatic phrase.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): with great.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000073369","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>She has the rare ability (1)/ of making complex theories (2)/ sound simple (3)/ and intuitively clear. (4) [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Ability” is followed by the infinitive “to + base verb.”</b><br>Part (2) should read “<b>to make</b> complex theories,” not “of making.”<br>“Make + object + adjective” correctly produces “make complex theories sound simple.”<br>The remaining parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000073370","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>What the consultant suggested implementing (1)/ was a method that would reduce redundancies (2)/ and optimize interdepartmental workflows (3)/ without requiring additional fundings. (4) [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Funding” is uncountable in the sense of financial resources.</b><br>Part (4) should read “additional <b>funding</b>,” not “fundings.”<br>The method would reduce redundancy and optimize workflows without extra financial support.<br>The other parts are grammatically sound.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): (4).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000073371","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>They are building a new bridge across the river. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A new bridge is built across the river by them."},"2":{"en":"A new bridge has been built across the river by them."},"3":{"en":"A new bridge is being built across the river by them."},"4":{"en":"A new bridge was being built across the river by them."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present continuous passive = is/are being + past participle.</b><br>The singular object “a new bridge” takes “is being built.”<br>A changes to simple present, B to present perfect, and D to past continuous.<br>“By them” correctly retains the agent.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): A new bridge is being built across the river by them.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000073372","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>The opposition is expected to challenge the ruling in court. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It was expected that the ruling would be challenged in court."},"2":{"en":"The ruling is expected to be challenged in court by the opposition."},"3":{"en":"Challenging the ruling is expected by the opposition."},"4":{"en":"The opposition was expected to be challenging the ruling."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Is expected to + verb” becomes “is expected to be + past participle.”</b><br>The object “the ruling” becomes the subject.<br>Correct form: “The ruling <b>is expected to be challenged</b> in court by the opposition.”<br>A changes the tense; C uses an awkward gerund subject; D retains the opposition as subject.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The ruling is expected to be challenged in court by the opposition.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000073373","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>He said that nothing but sheer luck could have saved them that day. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“Only sheer luck saved them that day,” he said."},"2":{"en":"“Sheer luck might have saved them that day,” he said."},"3":{"en":"“Nothing but sheer luck could have saved us that day,” he said."},"4":{"en":"“Only good fortune was with them that day,” said he."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Restore the speaker’s inclusive first-person plural “us” and the exact emphatic wording.</b><br>“Nothing but” and “could have saved” must remain unchanged.<br>A removes the modal and inclusive pronoun; B changes “could” to “might” and weakens “nothing but.”<br>D paraphrases and changes the modal structure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): “Nothing but sheer luck could have saved us that day,” he said.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000073374","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate synonym of the underlined word.<br>The trespasser remained <u>obstinate</u> despite repeated warnings. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Flexible"},"2":{"en":"Stubborn"},"3":{"en":"Gentle"},"4":{"en":"Obedient"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Obstinate (हठी) = stubbornly refusing to change one’s behaviour or opinion.</b><br><b>Flexible (लचीला)</b> = willing to adapt<br><b>Stubborn (जिद्दी)</b> = determined not to yield ✔<br><b>Gentle (सौम्य)</b> = mild and kind<br><b>Obedient (आज्ञाकारी)</b> = willing to obey<br>More synonyms: unyielding, headstrong, intransigent.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Stubborn.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000073375","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"The following sentence has been divided into four parts (P, Q, R, and S). The last part (S5) is fixed. Rearrange the remaining parts to form a grammatically correct and meaningful sentence, and choose the correct sequence.<br>P: been able on more than one occasion to verify Professor Clark's observations in regard to<br>Q: nerve-tissue is found in all animals above and including Hydrozoa according to Romanes, but<br>R: I am inclined to believe that it is present in animals even lower than Hydrozoa because I have<br>S: the protozoan “Stentor Polymorphus”, which has a well-developed nervous system, and I have<br>S5: moreover seen unquestionable acts of conscious determination enacted by this little creature. [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RPQS"},"2":{"en":"PSRQ"},"3":{"en":"SQPR"},"4":{"en":"QRPS"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QRPS</b><br>Q presents Romanes’s claim about nerve-tissue, and R introduces the writer’s contrasting belief.<br>P continues “because I have been able … to verify … observations in regard to.”<br>S identifies the protozoan and leads directly into the fixed S5.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): QRPS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000073376","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>In a narrow street inhabited by struggling artists, two young artists, Sue and Johnsy, lived together in a modest apartment. During a severe winter, Johnsy contracted pneumonia and gradually lost both her strength and her desire to recover. From her bed, she could see an old ivy vine clinging to the wall of a neighbouring building. As the cold wind tore away its leaves, she developed the strange belief that her life would end when the final leaf fell.<br><br>Sue tried to dismiss this belief as irrational, but Johnsy continued to watch the vine with increasing despair. An elderly painter named Behrman lived downstairs. Although he had spoken for years about producing a masterpiece, he had never created anything that fulfilled his ambition. When Sue told him about Johnsy’s condition, he appeared angry at her superstition but was deeply concerned.<br><br>That night, a violent storm swept through the city. By morning, Johnsy expected the vine to be completely bare. Yet one leaf remained firmly attached to the wall. It survived another day of wind and rain. Its apparent endurance stirred something within her. She began to feel ashamed that a fragile leaf could resist the storm while she had surrendered hope.<br><br>Johnsy slowly recovered. Sue later revealed that the leaf was not real. Behrman had painted it on the wall during the storm and had died of pneumonia soon afterwards. His masterpiece was never displayed in a gallery, but it restored a human being’s will to live.<br><br><br>What does Johnsy’s belief about the falling ivy leaves reveal about her mental condition? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She had become indifferent to Sue’s concern."},"2":{"en":"She had linked her survival to an irrational belief."},"3":{"en":"She had misunderstood the cause of her illness."},"4":{"en":"She had lost confidence in medical treatment."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Johnsy’s despair takes the form of a morbid superstition.</b><br><i>“She developed the strange belief that her life would end when the final leaf fell.”</i><br>She irrationally connects her survival to the vine.<br>Indifference to Sue, misunderstanding pneumonia and distrust of treatment are not stated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): She had linked her survival to an irrational belief.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000073377","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>In a narrow street inhabited by struggling artists, two young artists, Sue and Johnsy, lived together in a modest apartment. During a severe winter, Johnsy contracted pneumonia and gradually lost both her strength and her desire to recover. From her bed, she could see an old ivy vine clinging to the wall of a neighbouring building. As the cold wind tore away its leaves, she developed the strange belief that her life would end when the final leaf fell.<br><br>Sue tried to dismiss this belief as irrational, but Johnsy continued to watch the vine with increasing despair. An elderly painter named Behrman lived downstairs. Although he had spoken for years about producing a masterpiece, he had never created anything that fulfilled his ambition. When Sue told him about Johnsy’s condition, he appeared angry at her superstition but was deeply concerned.<br><br>That night, a violent storm swept through the city. By morning, Johnsy expected the vine to be completely bare. Yet one leaf remained firmly attached to the wall. It survived another day of wind and rain. Its apparent endurance stirred something within her. She began to feel ashamed that a fragile leaf could resist the storm while she had surrendered hope.<br><br>Johnsy slowly recovered. Sue later revealed that the leaf was not real. Behrman had painted it on the wall during the storm and had died of pneumonia soon afterwards. His masterpiece was never displayed in a gallery, but it restored a human being’s will to live.<br><br><br>Which factor most seriously obstructed Johnsy’s recovery? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Her psychological surrender to a morbid superstition"},"2":{"en":"Her inability to receive continuous medical attention"},"3":{"en":"Her prolonged exposure to severe winter weather"},"4":{"en":"Her dissatisfaction with her life as a struggling artist"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>The chief obstacle is loss of hope, not lack of medical care.</b><br><i>“Johnsy … gradually lost both her strength and her desire to recover.”</i><br>Her belief that the last leaf would mark her death deepens this surrender.<br>Medical attention, exposure and artistic dissatisfaction are not identified as recovery obstacles.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Her psychological surrender to a morbid superstition.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000073378","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>In a narrow street inhabited by struggling artists, two young artists, Sue and Johnsy, lived together in a modest apartment. During a severe winter, Johnsy contracted pneumonia and gradually lost both her strength and her desire to recover. From her bed, she could see an old ivy vine clinging to the wall of a neighbouring building. As the cold wind tore away its leaves, she developed the strange belief that her life would end when the final leaf fell.<br><br>Sue tried to dismiss this belief as irrational, but Johnsy continued to watch the vine with increasing despair. An elderly painter named Behrman lived downstairs. Although he had spoken for years about producing a masterpiece, he had never created anything that fulfilled his ambition. When Sue told him about Johnsy’s condition, he appeared angry at her superstition but was deeply concerned.<br><br>That night, a violent storm swept through the city. By morning, Johnsy expected the vine to be completely bare. Yet one leaf remained firmly attached to the wall. It survived another day of wind and rain. Its apparent endurance stirred something within her. She began to feel ashamed that a fragile leaf could resist the storm while she had surrendered hope.<br><br>Johnsy slowly recovered. Sue later revealed that the leaf was not real. Behrman had painted it on the wall during the storm and had died of pneumonia soon afterwards. His masterpiece was never displayed in a gallery, but it restored a human being’s will to live.<br><br><br>How does the passage redefine Behrman’s idea of a “masterpiece”? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It presents artistic greatness as the result of technical perfection."},"2":{"en":"It suggests that public recognition is essential to establish artistic value."},"3":{"en":"It shows that artistic success depends on faithfully imitating nature."},"4":{"en":"It associates artistic greatness with the power to restore human hope."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>A masterpiece is valued by its life-restoring effect rather than public display.</b><br><i>“His masterpiece was never displayed in a gallery, but it restored a human being’s will to live.”</i><br>This makes compassion and restored hope the measure of artistic greatness.<br>Technical perfection, recognition and imitation of nature are not the passage’s criteria.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): It associates artistic greatness with the power to restore human hope.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000073379","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>In a narrow street inhabited by struggling artists, two young artists, Sue and Johnsy, lived together in a modest apartment. During a severe winter, Johnsy contracted pneumonia and gradually lost both her strength and her desire to recover. From her bed, she could see an old ivy vine clinging to the wall of a neighbouring building. As the cold wind tore away its leaves, she developed the strange belief that her life would end when the final leaf fell.<br><br>Sue tried to dismiss this belief as irrational, but Johnsy continued to watch the vine with increasing despair. An elderly painter named Behrman lived downstairs. Although he had spoken for years about producing a masterpiece, he had never created anything that fulfilled his ambition. When Sue told him about Johnsy’s condition, he appeared angry at her superstition but was deeply concerned.<br><br>That night, a violent storm swept through the city. By morning, Johnsy expected the vine to be completely bare. Yet one leaf remained firmly attached to the wall. It survived another day of wind and rain. Its apparent endurance stirred something within her. She began to feel ashamed that a fragile leaf could resist the storm while she had surrendered hope.<br><br>Johnsy slowly recovered. Sue later revealed that the leaf was not real. Behrman had painted it on the wall during the storm and had died of pneumonia soon afterwards. His masterpiece was never displayed in a gallery, but it restored a human being’s will to live.<br><br><br>What psychological change does the apparent survival of the last ivy leaf bring about in Johnsy? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She begins to believe that nature controls the course of human life."},"2":{"en":"She becomes suspicious that the leaf has been deliberately preserved."},"3":{"en":"She feels ashamed of her defeatism and regains the will to survive."},"4":{"en":"She concludes that her illness is less serious than she had assumed."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>The leaf’s endurance awakens shame and renewed hope.</b><br><i>“She began to feel ashamed that a fragile leaf could resist the storm while she had surrendered hope.”</i><br>She rejects her defeatism and begins to recover.<br>She does not suspect preservation or reassess her illness medically.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): She feels ashamed of her defeatism and regains the will to survive.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000073380","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>In a narrow street inhabited by struggling artists, two young artists, Sue and Johnsy, lived together in a modest apartment. During a severe winter, Johnsy contracted pneumonia and gradually lost both her strength and her desire to recover. From her bed, she could see an old ivy vine clinging to the wall of a neighbouring building. As the cold wind tore away its leaves, she developed the strange belief that her life would end when the final leaf fell.<br><br>Sue tried to dismiss this belief as irrational, but Johnsy continued to watch the vine with increasing despair. An elderly painter named Behrman lived downstairs. Although he had spoken for years about producing a masterpiece, he had never created anything that fulfilled his ambition. When Sue told him about Johnsy’s condition, he appeared angry at her superstition but was deeply concerned.<br><br>That night, a violent storm swept through the city. By morning, Johnsy expected the vine to be completely bare. Yet one leaf remained firmly attached to the wall. It survived another day of wind and rain. Its apparent endurance stirred something within her. She began to feel ashamed that a fragile leaf could resist the storm while she had surrendered hope.<br><br>Johnsy slowly recovered. Sue later revealed that the leaf was not real. Behrman had painted it on the wall during the storm and had died of pneumonia soon afterwards. His masterpiece was never displayed in a gallery, but it restored a human being’s will to live.<br><br><br>What central irony is associated with Behrman’s final artistic act? [SSC CGL 10/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The work he considered temporary later brought him artistic fame."},"2":{"en":"The painting he created in secrecy was later displayed publicly."},"3":{"en":"The leaf appeared lifeless but became his most realistic creation."},"4":{"en":"The illusion that saved Johnsy’s life ultimately cost Behrman his own."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Irony: His life-saving artistic illusion leads to his own death.</b><br><i>“Behrman had painted it on the wall during the storm and had died of pneumonia soon afterwards.”</i><br>The painted leaf restores Johnsy’s will to live, while Behrman loses his life.<br>The passage denies him public fame or display, and realism is not the central irony.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The illusion that saved Johnsy’s life ultimately cost Behrman his own.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};